INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (1339, 79, 'activity', 'owner', NULL, 'description', '2026-10-19 02:31:05.398241+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{"to": {"value": "Owner ask, 2026-10-12: non-English prayer names read as sentences (ms renders Last third as a 3-word phrase meaning \"the last third of the night\"; Midnight as \"the middle of the night\") where English carries 2 words and 1 word. The owner''s rule: prayer names are table-column headers - the shortest context-correct form, everyone knows the context, drop the/of/the/night. The owner''s ms example: \"sepertiga malam\" for Last third. All 11 names, all five non-English catalogs, owner verifies the drafts (D42''s process). Load-bearing: job 39''s gates pin prayer names to the sourced values of research/prayer-names.json and cap them at 24 plain characters - the re-shortening re-sources that file or supersedes it by owner ruling; the per-locale width keys are widen-only, so shorter names need the width reset question answered by planning. AMENDED 2026-10-12 (autonomous run): D81 - three strings ruled (ms Last Third `Sepertiga malam` = the owner''s example verbatim; hi Midnight drop the adjective; th Last Third drop the particle phrase); every other name ruled already-shortest (so unchanged); the D42 in-planning pass is superseded to an audit-time veto per the owner''s instruction to plan READY without the owner''s; the sourced glossary is `shared/i18n/sourced-names.json` (the row''s research path no longer exists), two entries superseded by ruling; the width reset is answered as a key-family rename `prayer_max_name_width_` with old keys removed. OWNER INPUT 2026-10-12: so Midnight flagged — `Habeennimo dhexe` reads as \"middle of the night\", the glossary holds it low-confidence with no source, and the owner''s candidate is the Google output `saqbadh`; this supersedes the already-shortest blanket for that one string, the scope widens to four strings at the resume, and the exact form is sourced or owner-ruled (plan LOG.md carries the record)\n\nStatus note: 2026-10-13, audited: four names shortened under the header rule (D81, the owner''s ms example verbatim; hi and th mechanical drops; D83 so Midnight from the owner''s flag, planner-sourced), glossary superseded on the two sourced entries and gaining so''s first sourced Midnight entry, width cache reset by key rename so the reserve tightens; all other names byte-identical. Executed as 2.0.143/2.0.144 through one planner-ruled stop (the dist round-trip files are gitignored artifacts, proven by on-disk import runs); the two-reviewer audit fixed five findings at 2.0.147 (the crash-window test''s stale seed narration and locale-less fixture key, the two \"names never change\" comments now teaching the re-key rule, the usePrayer/Prayer internal English-width names, the two glossary provenance notes)\n\nNeeds first: #61, #63"}}', NULL);
