INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2187, 16, 'comment', 'owner', 'minor: components/modals/Help.tsx the fold reveal never reads the list''s scroll offset, so the rows-that-fit-never-move half of D142.12 holds only while the list sits at the top. The 3T''s 41px closed overflow keeps every positive reveal target above the closed scroll maximum, so no shipped geometry can trip it, but a list that overflows further (larger text, shorter viewport) can scroll a fitting bottom row into view, tap it, and still see the list jump up. Track the offset from onScroll and skip when the open bottom already sits inside the window.', NULL, '2026-10-19 17:52:01.198672+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2188, 16, 'comment', 'owner', 'Audit closed 2026-10-19: both reviews adjudicated. The shared finding (the fold guard read the viewport as the fold, so a scrolled list could jump backward for an answer already on glass) is fixed in 21a6a6b1 with red-first unit and wiring tests and a killed-mutation pass on both guards; the gate-scope nitpick stands as the plan specifies, the byte pins guarding the residue. Merged to uat as 6ca537b1 (2.1.5). Delivered: the widgets question with the owner''s two-line answer naming each platform''s extent (iOS first), the answer opening into view on every phone, glass-proven on the 3T.', NULL, '2026-10-19 18:01:14.980509+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (4677, 484, 'comment', 'owner', 'Blind review of 3062e3db. The change is sound in behaviour: all five layouts render and push, the statics, contract, renderer and push suites are green (351 tests), the widget module is at 100 percent line coverage, tsc and biome pass, and every locale''s layout 4 and 5 display name is layout 3''s own digit substituted (74 locales, no invented strings). The gallery tables in app.json and shared/i18n/native-strings.json agree key for key in all 74 locales, and the android resource names match.

suggestion: stores/__tests__/widgetSettingsSync.test.ts:325, 339, 343 - the refresh pushes eighteen kinds, nine per schedule (app.json carries eighteen widget entries, eight home plus ten lock), so "fourteen kinds" and "ten of the fourteen" both undercount. Write eighteen, and "ten of the eighteen"; the same total is stated as twelve at stores/__tests__/widgetFlagOff.test.ts:6 and stores/__tests__/widgetIo.test.ts:176.
suggestion: shared/__tests__/widgetLockRenderer.test.ts:463 - the ticking-digit centring guard still runs on layout 3 alone, but layout 5 ships the same Text(timerInterval:) with multilineTextAlignment(''center''), so deleting that modifier from layout 5 leaves the suite green. Loop the assertion over [renderTreeFor3, renderTreeFor5] and update the comment that says layout 2 is the only one without a countdown.
nitpick: shared/__tests__/widgetContract.test.ts:160-161 - the body comment still reads "The lock module holds three layouts ... leaves the other two unguarded" under a test that now walks five. Say five and the other four.
nitpick: stores/widget.ts:236 - "Pushes a fresh timeline to all ten widgets" describes a push that now reaches eighteen kinds. Say eighteen, or drop the number.
nitpick: widgets/LockPrayerWidget.tsx:6198-6208 - layout 3''s registration was left below the two new bodies, so the file exports 4, then 5, then 3, and the "One layout, two kinds" comment appears twice verbatim at 6198 and 6205. Move layout 3''s pair up to line 3741, immediately after its body, and drop the duplicate comment.

