INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2597, 271, 'comment', 'owner', 'REVIEW (blind):

Diff uat..HEAD read in full (plugin, suite, app.json/package.json, collisions allowlist; board.sql skimmed as generated). Suite re-run in the worktree: `yarn jest plugins/ --silent` = 22/22 pass, `npx tsc --noEmit` clean, biome on the two new files reports one info-level useLiteralKeys (below the `--error-on-warnings` gate, and it matches portraitOnlyIpad''s computed-key style).

- CONFIRMED plugins/duoLandscapeGate.js:68 - `module.exports.ALL_ORIENTATIONS` is dead: no consumer exists (the suite deliberately defines its own four-orientation literal and destructures only GATE_SOURCE and editAppDelegate), and scripts/find-unused-exports.py never scans plugins/, so the repo''s own dead-export tool cannot catch it. Delete the export.
- CONFIRMED README.md - the hard rule "update the README when a change adds a user-facing feature" is unmet: the spanning landscape window on a folding iPhone''s inner display is a user-facing feature, and the launch-folded-stays-letterboxed-until-relaunch limitation is exactly the kind the Known limitations section carries. Nothing in the diff reflects either.
- NOTE plugins/duoLandscapeGate.js:27 - the idempotence sentinel `contents.includes(GATE_SELECTOR)` treats any template-provided `supportedInterfaceOrientationsFor` as "gate already inserted": if a future Expo template ships its own override, the gate silently no-ops while the plist mod still grants all four orientations to every screen (fail-open, every iPhone rotates, no throw). Same silent-disarm shape if a future SDK stops consulting the app-delegate method under the scene life cycle. Keying the sentinel on the helper''s own signature (isDuoInnerDisplay) would close the template-drift half.
- NOTE plugins/duoLandscapeGate.js (GATE_SOURCE) - the override never calls super, and ExpoAppDelegate''s own implementation of the same method routes through ExpoAppDelegateSubscriberManager ("values from Info.plist unless a subscriber requested a different orientation"). Correct for this portrait-pinned product and harmless with today''s deps (no expo-screen-orientation installed), but a future Expo module requesting orientations through the subscriber manager would be silently ignored, with nothing pointing here.

Cleared by reading, not assuming: the fallback mask [.portrait, .portraitUpsideDown] exactly restores today''s runtime mask, because @expo/config-plugins Orientation.js emits the portrait pair for orientation "portrait" - no phone rendering changes. Version discipline holds: app.json and package.json move 2.1.33 to 2.1.37 in lockstep, one patch per untyped subject, and android/app/build.gradle is prebuild-generated from app.json (untracked here; check-version-discipline.js itself reads only app.json). The stock template (template.tgz) is scene-based and ExpoAppDelegate implements this exact method, so the override sits on supported plumbing; the generated ios/Athan/AppDelegate.swift in the worktree shows the gate correctly placed. The android resolutions are pinned by tests and no Android, widget, notification or UI-component file is touched.', NULL, '2026-10-20 05:24:02.100445+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
