INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2632, 280, 'comment', 'owner', 'GRILL: nine findings. The load-bearing repo claims were re-verified against the tree and they hold: the AppDelegate class-close marker in ios/Athan/AppDelegate.swift, both Info.plist orientation arrays portrait-only today, portraitOnlyIpad''s ~ipad pin (a separate plist key, so no clobber), app.json''s orientation "portrait" and the free seat directly after ./plugins/portraitOnlyIpad, the 62 zero-above clamp in shared/insets.ts, the 500pt centred column in Screen.tsx, the open ExpoAppDelegate seam at line 243, agent-device''s orientation command, e2e/README.md''s Gotchas, yarn validate, scripts/version-collisions-allowlist.json, and every app.config.ts resolution passing a new string plugin through untouched. The points arithmetic holds: 3+2+3+1 = 9 on the ticket and on subtasks 281-284, each step typed per the board''s device/code/docs values. The Step-1-before-2 ordering, the zero-code branch, and the bump-then-prebuild-then-build order all stand.

1. Files names a ref that does not exist. "Read from the lane/271 ref" - lane/271 is gone (deleted with the ruling, per row 271''s closing comment) and 271''s worktree is gone too; no ref matches. The four commits still sit unreachable in the object store (767bb1d9, aceab2fc, 825e832f, b8d1a358), readable by hash today and gone at the next gc. Fix: restore a read-only ref before dispatch (git branch lane/271 767bb1d9) or rewrite Files to name the hashes and mark them gc-fragile.

2. Step 1 never produces the tall hold if the orientation mapping runs the other way. The instrument step issues only landscape-left and landscape-right, expecting the tall 669x951 class from them; portrait and portrait-upside-down are never tried, although which command maps to the tall canvas is exactly what no row has measured. If both landscape commands land and the canvas stays wide, no named branch fires (nothing refused to rotate) and two implementers part ways: one calls Blocked, one improvises. Fix: issue all four orientation values on the open panel and transcribe the class each reports; the tall class from any one of them is the tall hold.

3. D5''s history contradicts the record it cites. "Row 271''s lane had no rotation command, which is why the tall hold read as beyond its instruments" - row 271''s closing revision records the portrait class as "not producible by rotation on this panel", that is, rotation was attempted and the panel refused. The plan''s central optimism (the tall class "expected") rests on calling that measurement an instrument artifact. Fix: reword D5 to the defensible claim - 271''s asks were portrait-direction only, the landscape-direction rotation is the untried instrument - or verify what 271 actually drove before resting the mechanism on it.

4. A tool refusal is not an OS refusal, and the fallback is never sequenced. Step 1 sends any "refusal to rotate" straight to the Blocked branch, but the owner''s pre-ruling reserves BLOCKED for the OS refusing the portrait-tall presentation. An agent-device command that errors or no-ops on the foldable is an instrument gap; D5 names Device Hub''s rotate buttons as the GUI fallback and no step ever routes to them. Fix: Step 1 tries the Device Hub fallback before any Blocked call on a command-level failure, and reserves Blocked for "the rotation lands and the canvas stays wide or letterboxed".

5. The wide-hold outcome closes Done on the plan''s own authority. D4 and Risk 5 let the natural wide hold present spanning landscape once the plist widens, record it, and proceed - shipping, in the Duo''s default posture, the rendering the owner cancelled with the recorded reason "no landscape in general - it would break the app''s flow". The ruling is silent on that outcome; the plan settles it itself. Fix: that outcome parks Awaiting Owner with the transcribed reading and screenshot for the owner''s call before Done.

6. Acceptance 4''s "screenshots of Option B on the row in both poses" is never met. Step 1 attaches the tall hold and the landscape-hold control (both open-pose holds); Step 3 attaches the tall hold only; no step attaches a closed-pose screenshot. Fix: attach the closed-pose control screenshot - its reading is already in Step 1''s list - and name in the plan the two poses that satisfy the criterion.

7. D6 mishandles the precedent it cites. Row 271''s grilled Decision 5 parks the row Awaiting Owner when an open-pose top inset exceeds 62; D6 transcribes the reading and proceeds to Done. Fix: park Awaiting Owner with the reading, matching the precedent, or record why this row differs.

8. The README fence is dropped. Row 271''s blind review ruled the equivalent rendering change user-facing and named the README rule unmet; this plan''s code branch ships a user-facing presentation change plus the D7 live-pose limitation with no README step anywhere. Fix: Step 4 (or 2) carries the README update on the code branch and records the zero-code branch''s exemption.

9. Three of row 271''s one-liners fell out silently. The app.json edit rides the repo''s ask-first rule with no recorded consent basis (271''s Decision 2 recorded the owner''s cover for the plugins-list entry; D3 assumes it). The main tree''s gitignored android/app/build.gradle is hand-set to the merged version after merge (271''s Files; /android is ignored, so prebuild -p ios never touches it) while Steps and Files name only package.json and app.json. And Step 3 drops the half-open transcription 271''s grill forced into its Step 2, with no reason given. Fix: one consent line in D3, one hand-set line in Step 4, and restore the half-open line or record why the tall canvas cannot see that pose.

Board integrity, fixed on sight per the workflow: removed the stale relation that had Done row 271 blocking this row (it was added after 271 closed; a completed ticket blocks nothing).', NULL, '2026-10-20 05:39:16.15955+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
