INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2724, 280, 'comment', 'owner', 'REVIEW (plan-conformance): the change follows the plan as amended by the owner''s four binding rulings of 2026-10-20, and the ruled branches were taken, plainly: D3''s four-orientation plist maximum did NOT land - the plugin pins the portrait pair on both arrays with the full-screen key (plugins/duoTallCanvas.js:33-38) plus the AppDelegate gate answering the portrait pair for every window, which is the lock the no-wide-layout ruling orders, so D4''s Awaiting-Owner park can never fire (the portrait declaration cannot present landscape); D6''s no-JS-change is overruled and shared/insets.ts:18-19 gains the width arm, so the 2.1.24 clamp no longer eats the tall canvas''s measured 82 - one code path, no Duo-specialised value, no new constant (PHONE_MAX_TOP_INSET and SIZE.contentMaxWidth both pre-existing, shared/constants.ts untouched); the closed pose is untouched (inset 0 takes the identity arm, measured readings identical across builds). Verified in the worktree: yarn validate green at 100 percent coverage (228 suites, 5885 tests); the lane-only diff is exactly the plugin, its suite, the clamp, its suites and wiring, README, the version files and the snapshot; one patch per commit in lockstep, 2.1.34 through 2.1.37, expected below uat''s 2.2.x until the merge takes the next free version; ios/ and android/ are gitignored so the plugins layer is the committed truth; no lane/271 content anywhere; both poses'' screenshots exist on the row and the wide-hold trade-off is tabled, never filled. Findings:

1. CONFIRMED - plan Files, "board/snapshot/board.sql regenerated per commit": only 2.1.34 regenerated it; 2.1.35, 2.1.36 and 2.1.37 carry no snapshot, so the branch HEAD''s board.sql predates all four owner rulings and the step 2 and 3 records (it carries step 1''s records only). One board/snapshot.sh run in the merge commit closes it.

2. minor - plan Step 4: the closing record names the plugin, its suites, README and the version files but omits board/snapshot/board.sql (which the branch diff does carry) and the post-merge gitignored android/app/build.gradle versionName hand-set the step was to name.

3. minor - subtask T-284 (Step 4) sits in Backlog though its commit landed at 2.1.37; tick it before Done.

4. NOTE - the gated build''s wide hold was never measured directly (rotation is the owner''s on this host); the tabled trade-off rests on step 1''s reading of the same portrait-pair plus full-screen plist shape, and the gate only narrows the delegate answer, so the letterbox stands. Sound, and recorded as tabled rather than hacked.

5. nitpick - comment 2720''s "standard 13 offset" names the visual text top (y=95 = 82 plus 13), not SCREEN.paddingTop 17 that the formula and the tests pin (99 = 82 plus 17, __tests__/app/Screen.test.tsx). The phones''-formula claim itself is test-pinned.', NULL, '2026-10-20 11:30:06.347395+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (2725, 280, 'comment', 'owner', 'REVIEW (blind): No defects found. The branch''s own diff (merge-base 4b6c577a..lane/280) is exactly the orientation plugin and its suite, the inset clamp and its suite, Screen''s one-line consumption and its suite, README, the two version files and the board snapshot; everything else the two-dot diff shows is uat''s post-fork work reversed, not this change.

Evidence: the three touched suites pass 26/26 with none skipped and the named tests confirmed running; yarn validate green (228 suites, 5885 passed, 1 skipped - the skip is the pre-existing conditional audioMatrix test, present at the merge base); tsc --noEmit clean and biome clean on all six touched files. Red-first holds: the old one-argument clamp body is literally the no-width-guard mutant and fails three of the new suite''s expectations, and all four clamp guard mutants die. The clamp reuses PHONE_MAX_TOP_INSET (62) and SIZE.contentMaxWidth (500), so no new layout constant and one consumption path. The plugin''s plist pin writes the same portrait pair Expo''s orientation:"portrait" and portraitOnlyIpad already write, and its UIRequiresFullScreen matches app.json''s existing requireFullScreen, so it is pure drift-pinning; the sentinel keys on the gate mask, is idempotent, and throws on marker drift. uat''s newer app.config.ts still consumes the app.json plugin list, so the seating survives the merge. Version lockstep holds on every commit (2.1.33 through 2.1.37, package.json and app.json together). The four privacy-manifest terms were decoded from uat''s manifest and scanned: zero hits across the branch tree, the committed snapshot and the diff; no console.log, no identifiers. Two minor items:

NOTE board/snapshot/board.sql (commit 10e46456): the snapshot is a mid-run capture from before uat''s 2.2.4 privacy-regime rewrite of snapshot.sh, committed in the branch''s first commit while the records-close commit''s claims postdate it. It carries no manifest term, but it will conflict with uat''s regenerated snapshot at the merge: resolve by regenerating, never hunk-by-hunk, and land the fresh snapshot in the run''s closing commit.

nitpick: plugins/duoTallCanvas.js:39-44: the composed withDuoTallCanvas and its callback are executed by no test (plugins/ sits outside jest''s collectCoverageFrom; scoped coverage shows the two edit functions covered, the composer not), so a wiring slip such as a dropped return cfg would pass yarn validate and corrupt the prebuild product. The worktree read-back is today''s only proof for that wiring; the sibling replacePreviousNotification shares the shape, so this is convention-consistent, and a suite that runs the composed plugin over a stub config would close it.', NULL, '2026-10-20 11:32:34.49859+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
