INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3109, 294, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 3 done: the row veil, the ago badge and the info box layer fade now carry their text through colour - the rows and the badge sink their ink (and the badge its pill) toward one ruled veil solid, #0b0016, and drop from display once the fade has run; the info box fades its text-free card face while the title and body inks rise from the card surface. The mechanism is argued twice in plan doc T-294, the sweep''s pending entry is gone, and yarn validate is green on lane/294 (e3d3bf9d, 2.4.14). Left: Step 4, the device reads on the owner''s mock build of the branch, then the merge.', NULL, '2026-10-21 15:24:10.680651+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3110, 294, 'comment', 'owner', 'Plan-conformance audit of lane/294 (4249bade, 1898bdc3, e3d3bf9d) against plan doc T-294. The code conforms: every A1-A6 and B1-B9 site is converted exactly as the plan''s tables specify, all sixteen tabled solids match value for value (muted #52529e, rowTime #5a5fa6, secondary #6c79c2, timeColon #5f60ad, nextTimeColon #a9b1de, extras #d7d9ef, prayerAgo #5660a7, sheetSubtitle #416899, disabled #6392ba, qibla inks #4e648e/#8d7662, SoundItem pair #8695d5/#416899, Help trio #76828e/#acb3bb/#727e8f, FAINT_BLUE #bbc3d7, grabber #5b77a4, veil #0b0016), the disabled state matrix in dim.ts matches the plan cell for cell, the three veil fades follow both argued Step 3 decisions with resting frames pinned by tests, the ruled-out list carries only view and icon opacity, the gradient is untouched, the dead hooks left with their last consumers, and the versions step 2.4.12/13/14. Three findings:

major: components/__tests__/textInk.test.ts:205 - the sweep''s opacity arm checks only the tag''s own style expression, so a Text styled through a named StyleSheet entry carrying opacity stays green, even though the colour arm does walk the referenced entries and the header claims "the styles it names" are checked; that named-entry shape is exactly what A2 and A3 were before conversion. Fix: run the same opacity regex over referencedEntries() in the opacity arm.

minor: components/sheets/parts/dim.ts (SEGMENT_PILL, CONTROL_WASH) - the plan''s decision says the stepper wash and segment pill "keep an equivalent opacity on a text-free subtree so their pixels hold exactly" (which ColorPicker''s dot and border did, previewDim 0.25); the code pre-flattens them to per-state solids instead. Pixels verified identical either way (rest equals the old interactive.active and the old rgba wash), so confirm the flatten as the chosen equivalent or carry the opacity as ruled.

nitpick: components/overlay/Overlay.tsx:23 - the header comment still says the layer owns the extras explanation box "faded by a derived opacity"; this change made that clause false (the box now reveals through the card face and rising inks), so drop it.', NULL, '2026-10-21 15:36:34.25596+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3111, 294, 'comment', 'owner', 'Blind audit of lane/294 at e3d3bf9d. The conversions are sound where I could recompute them: every flattened solid I checked against its stated base (sheetSubtitle #416899, sound inks #8695d5/#416899, help body/chevron on the white card, faint blue, grabber #5b77a4, the colon trio, the CONTROL_WASH and reminder tables under the old 0.125/0.2/0.15 stacks, the pill resting on interactive.active) reproduces exactly, the hold-then-hide drops sit on fixed-height containers so no layout shifts, useDerivedProgress''s first-evaluation snap keeps every new tween first-frame settled, and the veil composition stays solid end to end. Four findings:

major: components/__tests__/textInk.test.ts:205 - the opacity check runs only on the tag''s inline style expression; a Text pointing at a StyleSheet entry that sets opacity (style={styles.faded}) passes the sweep untouched, because referencedEntries feeds only the colour-alpha walk at line 219. The acceptance "no Text or Animated.Text carries opacity (style or animated style)" is therefore not proven for sheet-referenced opacity, the most likely shape a future regression takes. Fix: run the same /[{,]\s*opacity\s*:/ regex over the referenced entries, not just the inline expression.

major: shared/constants.ts:860 - qibla away.ink ''#4e648e'' is not the flatten its comment claims: rgba(146,184,228,0.45) over the away face (54,44,62) is #5f6b89. QiblaCompass.tsx:150 still applies fillOpacity 0.5 (FACE.cardinalInk), so #5f6b89 is also the pixel-preserving solid; with #4e648e the away cardinal digits composite #4b4c63 -> #424866, a real shift on a settled visual. Fix: set #5f6b89 (or record the owner''s ruling for the hand value and rewrite the comment).

major: shared/constants.ts:872 - facing.ink ''#8d7662'' is exactly the old rgba(228,192,134,0.5) flattened over the away face, while its comment names the facing face; over (66,53,72) the flatten - and the pixel-preserving solid under fillOpacity 0.5 - is #937b67. The copy of the base colour between the two palettes looks like the slip. Fix: set #937b67.

question: components/sheets/screens/QiblaCompass.tsx:150 - the cardinal digits are SVG Text whose dimming still rides fillOpacity 0.5 after this change, i.e. text rendering through an opacity the sweep cannot see (no style prop, element-level prop). Is the compass deliberately outside the sweep''s scope? Carrying the 0.5 into the solid and dropping fillOpacity finishes the invariant; if it stays, the scope line in the test''s header should say so.

minor: components/sheets/parts/SoundItem.tsx:80 - countdownColorProgress is a bare useDerivedValue returning withTiming, so on every remount (each play) it animates from 0 over 75ms; a selected row''s countdown now first-frames in the unselected ink, where the always-mounted version it replaces appeared settled. Fix: snap the first evaluation the way useDerivedProgress does.

nitpick: components/sheets/parts/index.ts:1-10 - the dim re-exports are dead weight: SegmentedControl, Stepper, ReminderCard and the sweep all import from parts/dim directly, and nothing imports them through the barrel. Drop the block or route the consumers through it, one or the other.', NULL, '2026-10-21 15:40:55.207115+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3112, 294, 'comment', 'owner', 'Audit closed: both reviewers'' findings confirmed and fixed in one commit (3427a3b0, 2.4.15) - the qibla cardinals'' inks were flattened over the wrong faces and now carry the full flatten at fill opacity 1 with the 0.5 fillOpacity deleted, the sweep gained the named-entry, fillOpacity and case-insensitive-resolver arms (each gap proven red first), the sound row''s countdown snaps on first evaluation, and two hygiene bits. The plan doc''s qibla table is corrected and the audit section records it. Step 4 (the mock build and 3T install for the owner''s read) is running.', NULL, '2026-10-21 15:52:22.137053+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
