INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3281, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 1 done: the tip''s numbers are measured, and every audited interaction on 2.4.24 fails the 30fps floor. The bisect steps own which commits brought it.

Build: Release gate-ON at uat tip 1c22014c, com.example.athan, versionName 2.4.24, versionCode 1000000, EXPO_PUBLIC_PERF_MONITOR=1, dev/mock env, arm64-v8a; aapt2 badging asserted per D8, installed on the 3T at User 0 alone, first post-install launch discarded, PERF_MEASURE lines verified flowing before any drive.

Marks against e2e/baselines/android-3t.json (medians, n=10 each): none regressed. overlay_open 139 and overlay_close 158.5 against the 240 entries (below the s9 instrument band the baseline''s own note says never to judge by), sheet_alert_open 434.5 vs 456, sheet_settings_open 382 vs 370, sheet_settings_close 209.5 vs 202; sheet_alert_close 209.5 has no baseline entry. The owner-visible regression is entirely in the frames, not the marks.

Frame audits, video path, all four FAIL the 30fps floor. overlay-open: a 671ms hole after the tap before anything draws, the layout then lands in one jump and 280ms of smooth scale+dim follows; its 1053ms and 425ms gaps are settled-idle (vision proved identical pixels across them). overlay-close, through frame-audit.sh''s new pre-tap open mode: about 300ms tap-to-first-draw dead zone, then the close ramp is monotonic at 19-37ms cadence; a mock data refresh hard-cut mid-recording. sheet-alert-open: eight gaps over 33ms, 84 to 482ms. sheet-settings-open: the sheet snaps - it first appears already 96.4 percent traveled (1579 of 1638px in one step) and crawls the last 59px over 67ms, after a 591ms dead zone from tap to first draw.

Vision verdicts: motion is monotonic wherever frames actually drew, with no ghosting or squash anywhere; the failures are dead zones after the tap and, for the settings sheet, an entrance that does not render at all. The alert sheet''s own vision read is still pending; its printed gap list stands as evidence.

Device state for the record: the 3T was found with a stale Android Studio screen-sharing agent at 100 percent CPU for about 36 hours (killed, the plan''s named risk), battery at 6 percent on a slow charge throughout with battery saver off, and after a mid-session reboot the phone sat locked behind OnePlus''s pocket-mode guard, which voided two early overlay runs (zero marks); all numbers above come after unlocking. Harness finding: the committed sheets-x10 flow''s settings tap (540,1730) is stale on this layout - the live tree puts the Settings button''s center at (539,1833) and the flow''s point lands on empty gradient, so the first BACK exits the app and the run measures nothing; the sheets measurement drove a corrected copy (that one coordinate) from the session temp dir, and the committed flow needs the fix in a later step. Evidence dirs, worktree-local and untracked because device frames never commit: e2e/evidence/ overlay-open-221800, overlay-close-221829, sheet-alert-open-221857, sheet-settings-open-221924, baseline-overlay-x10-220442, baseline-sheets-x10-221800. The harness change is committed at 2.4.25 (4ffd1f34): frame-audit.sh''s pre-tap open mode, with the 2.4.25 duplicate against lanes T-336 and T-337 allowlisted under the standing collision ruling.', NULL, '2026-10-24 21:33:56.144848+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3282, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'The alert sheet''s vision read has since landed and completes the record: after its first drawn step the entrance is genuinely monotonic (a decelerating 160,118,84,56,34,16,6,1 px descent sampled at 15-18ms, rigid, no ghosting or squash), but that first step covers 71 percent of the 1632px travel in one frame, and the scrim jumps 55 percent then holds 33ms before the sheet moves - the same unrendered-entrance failure as the settings sheet, less extreme. All four verdicts above stand.', NULL, '2026-10-24 21:34:21.818545+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, 3281, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3283, 337, 'comment', 'owner', 'Step 2 done. The prod iOS build of the lane tip installed on the XS and carried through the first sync, the bell enabling and the midnight rollover; the phone now sits foregrounded on the Standard page for Step 3.

Build and install: Release xcodebuild for a generic device, paid team inline, finished 22:38:28 BST after 5m15s, the API key verified present in the bundle by exact search (never printed); installed over the previous mock build at 23:00.

First sync, 23:01:46 BST: the Standard page read Sun 25 Oct - Fajr 05:04, Sunrise 06:39, Dhuhr 11:50, Asr 14:17, Maghrib 16:50, Isha 18:17 - equal to the API''s own 25 October values transcribed in Step 1, countdown 7h 2m to Fajr. Real times served, the mock''s rows gone. A finding for the later steps: the day label and lists move to the next day once the day''s last prayer has passed, not at midnight - my first read at 23:01 already showed 25 October, so the plan''s "Sat to Sun move at 00:00" does not exist as a midnight event on this build.

Bells: prior state recorded from the glyphs and the sheet - Standard Fajr off, Sunrise off, Dhuhr sound, Asr sound, Maghrib sound, Isha off, both reminders off (read in Fajr''s sheet); Extras Midnight, Last Third, Suhoor and Duha all off. The off rows are now Silent on both schedules (bells on, no 05:04 audio blast), the sound rows untouched, with one relaunch at 23:12:49 after the changes so the launch listener re-armed. After relaunch: Standard three bells and three speakers, Extras four bells.

Pre-crossing reads: Standard at 23:45:31 - day Sun 25 Oct 2026, countdown Fajr 6h 18m, all six rows equal to the oracle. Extras at 23:55:09 - day Sun 25 Oct 2026, countdown Midnight 2m 52s, rows Midnight 23:58, Last Third 01:00, Suhoor 04:44, Duha 06:59, all bells silent. The home screen (23:13) carries no widget, only the driver''s icon and the Athan dock icon, so the crossing''s home-screen read is recorded absent per the plan. The overlay (23:03): open on the Fajr row, the list below collapses away, the countdown carries onto the overlay.

Midnight rollover: at 23:57:59 the Extras countdown read Midnight 1s (zero never displays); by 23:58:07 it had flipped to Last Third 2h 1m against the row label 01:00 - two real hours to the 01:00 GMT instant across the duplicated hour, exactly as the static proof pins. At 00:03:01 Standard read Fajr 6h, continuous with 6h 18m at 23:45:31, name and day fixed; Extras at 00:03:23 read Last Third 1h 56m, a five-minute drop over the five minutes since 23:58:07. Day labels read Sun 25 Oct 2026 on both schedules throughout, having rolled early as above. No notification banner was visible in either frame at the 23:58:00 Midnight fire; silent delivery is not readable from the screen, so Step 5''s Fajr stays the fire proof.

The driver needed clearing first: a 17-hour-old session from a deleted lane worktree held both phones'' claims; the daemon was restarted and my own runner prepared with the paid team. The new traps are written back in the XS atlas (one commit, 2.4.26, allowlisted beside lane/322b under the standing ruling). The XS is unlocked, tethered, app foregrounded on Standard, runner installed.', NULL, '2026-10-24 23:25:47.799473+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
