INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3423, 327, 'comment', 'owner', 'Grill of the re-plan (doc v5), read against the repository and this row''s standing record. Four findings; what checked clean follows.

1. Steps 9, 10 and 14 (and D11) build on harness state that is not on uat. The pre-tap open mode was committed at 4ffd1f34 (2.4.25) per Step 1''s record, but that commit sits on no branch and is not an ancestor of uat; uat''s frame-audit.sh carries no such mode and no parameterised pre-tap wait, and the 1s close variant lived in session temp. Step 9 says the pre-tap settle "becomes a parameter" as though it exists. Step 9 must name the mode''s re-implementation (or the recovery of 4ffd1f34) as its own deliverable; otherwise Steps 10 and 14 have no overlay-close instrument to drive.

2. D12 contradicts the repository''s fleettest gate. AGENTS.md: before any install to a phone the owner uses, assert the badging and stop if the id is not the fleettest id. The owner personally uses the 3T (the verdict of 2026-10-25; the owner''s prod line lived on it), so the gate keys on the phone, not on the installed package as D12''s narrowing claims. D12 must either make the 3T installs fleettest-id builds or record the owner''s exemption for the dev-id line on that phone; as written, Step 10''s first install either stops at its own assert or breaks the repo rule.

3. D12''s measured builds contradict the owner''s same-day both-platforms order. AGENTS.md (owner order 2026-10-25): a one-platform build never happens, even when the change seems platform-specific; device builds go through build-prod.zsh and build-mock.zsh. The plan''s measured builds are the Android-only harness ritual, and the only both-platform path cannot emit marks (build-mock.zsh unsets EXPO_PUBLIC_* wholesale). The plan needs the owner''s explicit exemption for measurement builds, or each measurement session must compile iOS beside the Android build; D12 cannot split the build rules on its own.

4. Step 9 times the SF read wrong as written: "the latency dump reads the recent-frame ring buffer after the settle". A dump after the 12s settle lands before the tap: an idle layer presents nothing and the SF block prints NO DATA. The dump must land after the recorded animation (the existing SF branch''s shape: tap, then dump), and promptly, since the ring buffer holds only about 127 frames. Step 9 should say so in those words.

Checked clean: the points arithmetic (19 done plus 24 open equals 43, every subtask estimate matches its step); the anchor 6478619b exists on uat as 1.25.0 and carries mocks/simple.ts, e2e/README.md with the same build ritual, its own yarn.lock, and the same com.example.athan id; the flows'' APP_ID substitution breakage and stale tap points are exactly as the plan records; build-mock.zsh and shared/perf.ts behave as D12 claims; SurfaceFlinger --latency does give per-frame present timestamps for a named layer on this Android 9 phone and --list resolves the rotating names; every file the plan names exists.', NULL, '2026-10-25 08:01:41.254394+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
