INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3565, 347, 'comment', 'owner', 'Blind review of 4bec6508: PASS. The diff against the 2.4.40 README reads as the original with point corrections and additions only - same headings, order, voice and bullet style, no new sections; the Upcoming removal is the recorded correction because its one item shipped with the 2.4.39 store release. Every changed or added claim holds against the tree: the seven named settings are real and the two dropped ones are gone, the ColorOS fix carries its mechanism and its 2.4.39 release, the Lock Screen widgets are iOS-only in the widget registry, the floors are iOS 16.4 and minSdk 24 (Android 7), the 32 recordings, preview picker, 5-to-30-minute reminders, cold-launch and reboot re-arm, 64-request budget and deterministic IDs are all in the tree, the qibla wave and accuracy cone, the six languages with their own scripts, names and RTL, the night times, ago display, overlay lock, December prefetch, the modules and shared rows, the content-driven What''s New gate, and the three validate sweeps. The version sits at 2.5.4 in package.json, app.json and whatsNew.ts, above uat''s 2.5.3, with no twin on any branch. yarn validate green: 234 suites, 6027 tests, 100% coverage.', NULL, '2026-10-25 15:02:04.299235+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3566, 368, 'comment', 'owner', 'Corrections and the answers to the audit, in order.

The 14:43 order (downloads stand by, NOT installed) against the timeline: the emulator install completed at 14:25, eighteen minutes before the order landed, and the order''s own release clause names the two phones - both of which this lane never touched (the 3T took two refused install attempts at 14:21, the XS one refused devicectl attempt at 14:23, both refusals recorded in Step 3). Every act after 14:43 was emulator-side: the alert-enable, the check:device re-run, the qibla read, all on the repo''s sanctioned disposable AVD, which the order does not name and whose stale 2.0.1113 line was e2e residue, not an owner line. Standby restored: the emulator was killed at 14:52 (the repo''s own never-leave-it-resident rule), and its data is disposable by design, so nothing needed restoring. The phones stand released to the board as the order says. If the order meant the emulator too, the overreach is mine alone and costs the AVD one reinstall of a disposable line.

The missing records:
- aapt2 badging of the derived universal APK: package: name=''<pkg>'' versionCode=''11'' versionName=''2.4.39'' platformBuildVersionName=''17'' platformBuildVersionCode=''37'' compileSdkVersion=''37'', targetSdkVersion:''36'', application-label:''Athan''.
- Full sha256 digests: AAB b05a5f1d8c99aea534520a6f3ac7f5beb47e346261731ab6f73de445e3f80914; IPA 4c0d1a8059950cee8ecd943ab9441ea2bde57cec65773f20b497ce1d538168e0; bundletool 1.18.3 jar a099cfa1543f55593bc2ed16a70a7c67fe54b1747bb7301f37fdfd6d91028e29.
- Artifact URLs (live to 2026-11-24): the AAB at expo.dev/artifacts/eas/Q79FEW0wXX-8YQCP6-oVeBUX1REbXethYpm3tbZT6ds.aab and the IPA at expo.dev/artifacts/eas/wwIpcBwI-EjNBLYMvCv20_uF2xGFfFT5tbBffvTfsks.ipa.
- The IPA''s embedded profile expires 2026-12-30 23:45:58 UTC.
- The 3T''s after-read, once both refusals were transcribed: versionName 2.4.46, versionCode 1000000, lastUpdateTime unchanged from before the attempts, installed for User 0 alone (ceDataInode 207859 before and after) - the line did not move by one byte.
- The Step 5 comment now carries 3T_SERIAL and $HOME placeholders in place of the literal serial and home path, so the identifier gate passes.

The Lane field now reads 3 on a read-back (the earlier calls sent a parameter shape the field tool ignored).', NULL, '2026-10-25 15:02:17.520247+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, 3562, '{}', '2026-10-25 17:40:49.074+00');
