INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3960, 401, 'comment', 'owner', 'Plan grill (doc v1), six findings:

1. Proof (b) and Risks rotate the simulator with `xcrun simctl ui <udid> orientation left|right`. That subcommand does not exist on this rig: Xcode 27.1 (27A9275) `simctl ui` offers only appearance and increase_contrast, and no orient or rotate verb exists anywhere in simctl (checked `simctl help`, `simctl ui`, `simctl io`). The rotation proof and the does-not-reproduce check both ride on a command that cannot run. Fix: name a mechanism that provably rotates (the Simulator.app Rotate Device menu via osascript, verified first) and read portrait geometry from transcribed `simctl io <udid> screenshot` dimensions.

2. Proof (c) asks for "the iPhone plist keys in the read-back build byte-identical to the pre-change read-back", which contradicts the plan''s own candidate 2. If the crash rode the fossil shape, the pre-change read-back carries the unscoped full-screen key and no `~iphone` key (both on-disk plists verified), and the fix''s purpose is to change exactly that, so its success fails the criterion as written. Fix: pin the baseline to the T-377 key set, not to the pre-change read-back.

3. Proof (c) scopes the diff to "the orientation-path files listed above", but under candidate 3 the fix lands in `app/_layout.tsx` or a hook, files the Changes list never names (only the plugin and its test are there). One implementer blocks the merge for an unlisted file, another edits only the plugin and never fixes the JS thrower. Fix: scope criterion (c) to the files the transcript names, or add the conditional JS files to Changes.

4. Decisions claims "the run''s orders authorize the simulator-only expo route". No readable order carries that: not the repo, not the ticket, not ai/plans. The repo carries the owner''s standing order (2026-10-25) that a one-platform build never happens even for platform-specific changes. A stranger executing this plan must either break the standing order or halt. Fix: quote the authorizing order with its date and wording into the decision, or build both platforms per the standing ritual.

5. Decisions builds with `EXPO_PUBLIC_IOS_WIDGETS` "unset", but the main checkout carries a gitignored `.env` that sets it to 1 and the Expo CLI auto-loads `.env`, so the plain expo route run there compiles the widget extension in and contradicts the stated build shape. The premise holds only in a fresh worktree with no `.env`, and the decision names no build directory (the clean-worktree rule appears only under Risks). Fix: name the lane''s fresh worktree as the build site in the decision, or carry an inline `EXPO_PUBLIC_IOS_WIDGETS=0` on the command.

6. Files names `hooks/useInitialWidth.ts` "(if present)". It does not exist; the hooks directory carries `useWindowDimensions.ts`. The hedge defers a question one ls answers, and the real width hook goes unnamed. Fix: name `hooks/useWindowDimensions.ts` and drop the phantom.

Checked clean, not reported: points arithmetic (8 on the ticket, 3+2+3 on the subtasks), label order and type, the fossil-shape claims in both ios trees, the T-377 commits and the ee2defc2 worktree, the bundle id behind the simctl launch command, the editAppDelegate warm-tree throw, and the mock default env.', NULL, '2026-10-28 01:25:50.704208+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
