INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3848, 388, 'comment', 'owner', 'Blind review of the uat range (2.11.23, 2.11.24):
- defect: stores/sync.ts:144 - hasUsableDays answering its own failed read as true flips the launch with genuinely empty storage AND a failing read from the error screen to a blank home screen (bootstrap''s own catch proves the app survives into sync there), and that nothing-stored side is pinned by no row, though the commit says those sides keep the error screen the honest first-install landing. One row - stored empty plus getPrayerByDateString throwing - would settle whether hasData is truly wanted there.
- nitpick: stores/__tests__/syncFailureInjection.test.ts:239 - the row named for the downloaded-days write-back read actually rejects earlier, at readArmedDays (sync.ts:380, before any wipe), so the write-back read at sync.ts:127 is never rejected by any row; the table cell promises a step nothing injects.
- nitpick: stores/__tests__/syncFailureInjection.test.ts:358 - this row re-runs a hand-copied body of app/index.tsx:178''s effect, so the real wiring can regress while the row stays green; it matches today, but it is the one mimic in an arc whose cleanup claims none landed.
Checked and clean: the new warn lines match the file''s existing SYNC/WIDGET shapes, the rewritten sync.test.ts rows pin the new contract on both sides, the rig injects at real module and storage boundaries rather than mocks of sync itself, both suites pass here (124 tests), and both commits bumped all three tracked version files with the What''s New oracle intact.', NULL, '2026-10-27 15:53:53.918458+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3849, 388, 'comment', 'owner', 'Plan-conformance audit of the second fold (a5150f23 + 2fd3b6e6, merge 6686f3b7): conforms. The rig''s 25 rows walk the chain as the code really runs it, against wiring that exists (_layout''s triggerSyncLoadable, the listeners'' bare sync on return to active, the home screen''s own notification-refresh catch); each of the five named throwers is gated on hasUsableDays with both sides pinned, the two rewritten sync.test.ts rows keep the old throw under its true nothing-stored condition, the cleanup commit changes only the doc blocks and the dead initializer, the repo greps clean of the mimic, and validate runs green here at full coverage. Two nits:

nitpick: stores/sync.ts:269 - the January 1 ask''s prelude is a sixth real thrower the rig caught (its row is red without the new catch), and it is fixed warn-only without the hasUsableDays gate; the granularity is argued in the comment and fits the gap shape, but the record''s "five throwers, each gated" undercounts it, so a future reader matching the record would re-add the gate the gap shape needs gone.

nitpick: stores/__tests__/syncFailureInjection.test.ts:384 - the failed-read-answers-usable ruling has no row on its far side: a read failure over a genuinely empty cache completes hasData rather than reaching the error screen, and all three nothing-stored rows keep the read working, so that side rests on the code comment alone.', NULL, '2026-10-27 15:58:43.363404+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3850, 388, 'comment', 'owner', 'Audit PASS, fold 2 (lead, 2026-10-27): plan-conformance clean with two nits (comment 3849), blind one defect and two nits (comment 3851-era). All four adjudicated. Confirmed and fixed in 562880f8 riding 2.11.25: the failed-read-answers-usable far side is now pinned over an empty store (killed under the flip mutation); the write-back row''s spy is stateful so its rejection truly lands at the write-back read, its guarding warn pinned (killed under the no-throw mutation); and the record is corrected - the rig named SIX throwers, not five, the January 1 prelude being warn-only by design for the gap shape. Rejected: the hand-copplied wiring row already cites its source in its own comment, and exporting an inline effect is a refactor beyond the fold. The XS restore follows, then the ticket closes.', NULL, '2026-10-27 16:06:51.889123+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
