INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3859, 396, 'comment', 'owner', 'Grill of the plan doc (read against the repo at lane2/T-396, 562880f8):

FINDING (D1, stamps): the plan calls the iOS empty-results / unreadable-installed return a failure, but that path already writes the full-day success stamp (setPopupUpdateLastCheck(now) runs before the no-comparison return, manual calls included), so the line "a manual failure still writes nothing" is false for it and invites moving the stamp, which would change automatic-check behaviour the plan freezes. Fix: name the three write-nothing paths (store read false, Play unanswered, outer catch) and state the empty-results failure keeps its success stamp.

FINDING (risks, minor): "the default mock . . . would refund and break the spent-budget tests" is mechanically wrong - a mock omitting the failed field reads falsy and refunds nothing; the default must change because the bare pair is no longer a shape the data layer can return. Fix: reword that one line; the remedy (default becomes an up-to-date verdict) stands.

PASS: D1''s failed mapping walks clean against every return in device/updates.ts as it stands - throttle refusal false, Android answered either way false, Android unanswered true, iOS storeVersion===false true, empty-results/no-comparison true, both comparison verdicts false, outer catch true; app/index.tsx:149 reads result.modal alone, so the launch check is untouched.

PASS: the row''s machine covers every reachable triple - the no-verdict/verdict pair {modal:false, upToDate:false, failed:false} reaches the row only as Android update-found and rests idle with the budget spent, per D2; modal:true never co-occurs with failed:true, so nothing becomes contradictory.

PASS: suite-touch claims hold - updates.test.ts pins 16 toEqual result assertions (the plan''s ~15 is fair) and every one gains failed; the Settings default mock at line 103 is the bare pair and the two budget tests riding it (lines 499, 559) only keep meaning under the plan''s remedy; the rewritten failure test (line 486) is genuinely red today because the row settles idle on upToDate:false.

PASS: the key settings.updateCheckFailed is free in all six catalogs; the six drafts clear every mechanical gate in catalogGates.test.ts (key-set parity, token parity, length budget, echo, RTL-Latin); the lock hashes en.ts alone per locale, so "six in, then yarn i18n:lock" is the right procedure.

PASS: close.svg exists, symmetric, currentColor, same construction as check.svg (already imported elsewhere), so D5''s mirror claim holds; the red pair #dc2626/#ef4444 mirrors the landed green #16a34a/#22c55e exactly.

PASS: steps executable - coverage really is gated at 100 (jest.config.js), the 1+2+3=6 arithmetic is right, 2.11.26 follows 2.11.25 with origin fetched first, the bump list matches the checked-in surfaces (the gradle is prebuild-generated and absent from the tree), and nothing touches stores, notification logic, or a pixel the owner did not spec.', NULL, '2026-10-27 16:28:16.078218+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
