INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3978, 401, 'comment', 'owner', 'Audit (plan-conformance, merge 95047b2e at 2.11.37) - four findings for the owner and the lead:

question: the lane proceeded past the plan''s own stop: doc v5 Decisions say "If neither shape aborts, the lane stops and reports" and "a reproduction that does not crash on the simulator is a stop and a report, never a silent fix of a neighbour symptom"; neither shape aborted, so acceptance (a)''s transcribed stack naming the throwing code has no log line behind it - the fix targets the transcribed mechanism (a neighbour of the crash), honestly recorded but contrary to the plan''s text, so the owner rules the deviation ratified or unwound before Done.

question: acceptance (b) and the Goal''s "orientation stays portrait and stable through system rotation" are unmet by the lane''s own measurement - iPadOS 27 read as refusing every app-side portrait lock, so the shipped state through device rotation is the exact "iPad lays out landscape" outcome the plan''s Decisions rejected; the closing comment already parks the posture with the owner, and Done cannot precede that ruling.

suggestion: plugins/duoTallCanvas.js:54-57 and :10-12 - the SCENE_BLOCK comment says "the posture holds only by re-requesting portrait geometry" and the header says "no surface ever lays out wide", but the plan doc''s own Step 3 measurement says the geometry request is ignored against a rotated scene and the iPad window lays out wide through rotation; the comments assert behavior the ticket''s record disproves, so rewrite them to the measured limit or drop the block if the owner accepts wide layout.

nitpick: plan Proof (c) demanded the fixed build''s plist read-back as "PlistBuddy lines quoted in the doc"; Step 3 paraphrases the key values (absent full-screen key, ~iphone=true, portrait pair, all-four) with no quoted command output behind them.

Checked clean: the diff scope (plugin pair plus version files; the What''s New restamp is standing convention, /android is gitignored prebuild output whose versionName regenerates), the withFinalizedMod array-form wiring repair and the dangerous-first/finalized-last ordering both verified against the installed SDK, the 22-row suite green at the merge commit, the version line 2.11.32-2.11.37 alone, iPhone keys and posture unchanged, no visuals touched.', NULL, '2026-10-28 04:27:06.507653+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.issue_activity (id, issue_id, kind, actor_name, body, action, created_at, actor_user_id, initiative_id, reply_to_id, payload, edited_at) VALUES (3979, 401, 'comment', 'owner', 'Blind audit of b489817d..95047b2e. The surgery, the mod-wiring repair and the version trio all check out against the installed SDK, the Expo templates and the mod compiler; three findings:

suggestion: plugins/duoTallCanvas.js:144-169 - the mod wiring has no unit pin and jest never measures it (jest.config.js collectCoverageFrom carries no plugins/**), so the exact defect this change fixes - mods silently never registered - can return with a green suite; the wiring''s only check was a one-off manual prebuild read-back, against the full-coverage rule. A test invoking withDuoTallCanvas(config) and asserting two ios finalized mods land on the stack pins the array form.

question: plugins/duoTallCanvas.js:106 - the PIN_FLAG sentinel returns a warm AppDelegate untouched, so a tree the previous release produced (gate and pin, no carrier) silently never receives PortraitWindowController while the SceneDelegate edit does land on the same warm tree - a half-applied posture. The plugin throws loudly on the gate-without-pin shape; should this shape throw too? Sanctioned builds prebuild --clean or stamp-gate on the plugins tree hash, so nothing sanctioned hits it today.

question: plugins/duoTallCanvas.js:65 - the rode selector is API_DEPRECATED since iOS 26 (the 27.1 SDK headers point to windowScene:didUpdateEffectiveGeometry:); it measured firing on the iPadOS 27 sim, but when Apple stops calling it the scene half dies silently - the same silent-no-op shape this change spent five commits hunting. Worth recording the deprecation beside the measured finding, or pinning a fallback.', NULL, '2026-10-28 04:35:25.440398+00', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', NULL, NULL, '{}', NULL);
