INSERT INTO public.project_document (id, project_id, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, archived_by_ancestor_id, "position", version, owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, updated_by_user_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (36, 1, NULL, 'T-337', '# T-337 - The clocks fall back at 02:00 London: everything time-related rides the real transition whole

## Goal

Tonight, 2026-10-25 02:00 Europe/London, the clocks fall back to 01:00 (BST to GMT). The owner ordered a live proof that every time the app shows, arms or stores rides the real transition whole: display times and dates on both schedules, the overlay and the home screen, the countdown, the day rollover, the notification arming, and the stored rows. The plan is done when the static suites plus tonight''s transcribed device readings prove each acceptance criterion, or name the defect they caught.

The hard clock: the crossing is at 01:00 UTC (02:00 BST). All prep finishes by 01:30 device time. The live window is 01:45-02:20 device time.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-24 - The crossing device is the iPhone XS (`IPHONE_UDID`, resolved by `xcrun devicectl list devices`). The OnePlus 3T belongs to Lane 2 tonight and appears only as a lead-gated extension. Why: the dispatch constraint; on iOS the readings are the screen and the notifications themselves.
- 2026-10-24 - The four reading instants are 01:55:00 BST, 02:00:00 BST (= 01:00:00 GMT, the fall-back), then +5 and +15 real minutes, which the wall clock reads as 01:05 GMT and 01:15 GMT. Why: after a fall-back there is no wall 02:05 within minutes of the crossing; the dispatch''s "02:05 and 02:15" are taken as +5/+15 real minutes past the transition, not wall labels. Ruling returned to the lead.
- 2026-10-24 - The midnight rollover (00:00 BST, Sat 24 to Sun 25 Oct) is captured live inside the prep step, two hours before the fall-back. Why: the owner''s order names the day rollover, and tonight is the one night the rollover and the fall-back share a day.
- 2026-10-24 - The prep step turns both schedules'' at-time athan bells on when off and records the prior state; the restore happens in Step 6, after Step 5''s Fajr fire. Why: restoring earlier disarms the armed Fajr alert before it fires and would stage a miss the app did not cause; the fire-on-time criterion is unobservable with bells off.
- 2026-10-24 - In-app taps on the XS run through the atlas Driver route: the `agent-device` CLI with the iOS runner prepared (`AGENT_DEVICE_IOS_TEAM_ID=<paid team> agent-device prepare ios-runner --udid $IPHONE_UDID`), which installs two runner apps on the phone, uninstalled when the night ends. Leaving the app uses terminate or the app switcher, never the banned home/bottom-edge swipes. Why: the atlas is the measured route; snapshots wedge on the countdown, so every read is a screenshot via `pymobiledevice3 developer dvt screenshot`.
- 2026-10-24 - After any bell change the app is relaunched once before 01:30. Why: the sheet-dismiss commit path reschedules, and the launch listener is the second event that puts a refused prayer right; the relaunch makes the armed state certain whichever path carried the change.
- 2026-10-24 - A mock build is ruled out for every live step. Why: it serves launch-relative times and does not ride the real transition. All builds carry EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=prod with the key from `~/.config/athan/.api_key` exported into the build process env only, never printed, never written.
- 2026-10-24 - The only code that changes tonight is tests. A gap test that exposes a real defect is recorded on this ticket and fixed in a follow-up ticket after the crossing. Why: fixing inside the window invalidates the proof the owner ordered.
- 2026-10-24 - Static gap coverage, each test proven able to fail by a mutation pass (flip the guarded logic, watch it fail, revert) and never reading the real clock: (a) the London calendar date inside both passes of the duplicated hour, (b) notification candidate rows with now inside the duplicated hour, (c) countdown display continuity across the transition instant. Why: the suites pin the fall-back instant mapping, the night rows and real-elapsed countdown windows, but not these three with now inside the duplicated hour.
- 2026-10-24 - Version: executors fetch origin and take the next free patch above everything visible (`lane/322b` carries 2.4.26; 2.4.27 is the expected number), bumping `package.json`, `app.json` and `android/app/build.gradle` together even for an iOS-only build. Why: the version-bump rule is per commit, not per platform.
- 2026-10-24 - The home-screen widget: Step 2''s home-screen read records whether a widget sits on the XS home screen. When one does, the +5 reading transcribes it from the home-screen screenshot; when none does, that reading is recorded absent and nothing is installed inside the window. Why: the widget rides the same stored rows the lists read; installing one at 01:50 buys no evidence and costs window time.
- 2026-10-24 - Arming evidence on iOS is the bell-state screenshots plus the notifications that fire (the window''s fire at its instant and Step 5''s Fajr); the alarm dump belongs to the 3T extension alone. Why: iOS exposes no scheduled-notification dump, and the acceptance clause is read through that substitute.

## Files

Changed:
- `shared/__tests__/time.test.ts` - gap pins: the London date in both passes of the duplicated hour; countdown display continuity across 01:00 UTC.
- `shared/__tests__/notifications.test.ts` - gap pin: candidate rows and first still-due list day with now inside the duplicated hour.
- `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` - the version bump.
- `e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md` - written back when a route or trap is newly measured tonight.

Read, not changed: `e2e/README.md` and its Gotchas, `e2e/AGENTS.md`, `e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md`, `e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md` (only on the 3T extension), `$HOME/athan-gitree/bin/build-prod.zsh` (the prod env shape and the single-slot check), `shared/time.ts`, `shared/prayer.ts`, `shared/notifications.ts`, `stores/countdown.ts`, `stores/sync.ts`, `api/client.ts`, `api/config.ts`.

## Design

Approach: static proof first, one committed device through the whole night, findings recorded on the ticket as they happen.

What the suites already prove (verified 2026-10-24 by reading them):
- `shared/__tests__/time.test.ts` DST blocks: `createPrayerDatetime` maps pre-transition, duplicated and post-transition clock strings on 2026-10-25, choosing GMT (the later occurrence) inside the duplicated hour; spring-forward is pinned the same way.
- The autumn night rows: `getNightTimes(''2026-10-24'',''17:52'',''2026-10-25'',''05:04'')` pins Last Third at 2026-10-25T01:00:00Z, the second 01:00.
- The countdown window crossing the fallback counts the real 8.5h, not 7.5h; `getSecondsRemaining` is `max(1, ceil)`, so 0 seconds never displays.
- The London calendar date around winter and summer midnight; `yarn test:tz` runs the whole suite under four device timezones.
- `shared/__tests__/notifications.test.ts`: rows arm whole, in time order, until the 64-request budget; an unreadable row is never armed.

The live proof rides the invariant the code is built on: prayer times are true UTC instants rendered through PRAYER_TIMEZONE. The fall-back changes only the wall-clock label of every reading; no instant moves. Every device reading is compared against the API''s own served values, fetched once in Step 1 with the key read straight into the process environment.

The reading instants, both labels:
- R1 = 01:55:00 BST = 00:55:00 UTC (last minutes of the FIRST 01:xx wall pass).
- R2 = 02:00:00 BST = 01:00:00 UTC, the fall-back instant (bracketed with reads at wall 01:59:55 BST and 01:00:05 GMT).
- R3 = 01:05:00 GMT = 01:05:00 UTC (+5 real minutes; SECOND 01:xx wall pass).
- R4 = 01:15:00 GMT = 01:15:00 UTC (+15 real minutes).

R1 sits in the first 01:xx pass and R3/R4 in the second: the same wall labels occur twice, and the day label, list content and countdown target must agree across both passes. That is the duplicated-hour proof.

Countdown continuity, scoped: the Standard countdown renders minutes outside the final ten minutes of its target, so its displayed remaining drops exactly five minutes from R1 to R2 and five more from R2 to R3 while its target name and the day stay fixed. The Extras countdown at R1 targets the 25 Oct list''s Last Third row, whose real instant (from the API''s Maghrib 24 Oct and Fajr 25 Oct) lands within minutes of the transition: its flip to Suhoor across R2-R4 is its own expected reading, not a continuity breach. The Last Third row sits on the 25 Oct Extras list because night rows file under the day the night leads into - reading it there at R1 is the expected state, not a list roll.

Notification reads: a notification that fires inside the window is transcribed live from its banner; the phone is locked once after R4 and the lock-screen entries transcribed then. "Backgrounded" for the overnight steps means locked with the app foregrounded - the atlas bans the home and bottom-edge swipes.

Alternatives rejected:
- Mock build for the crossing: serves launch-relative times, does not ride the real transition.
- Setting a phone''s clock by hand to fake 02:00: the owner ordered the real transition; a clock jump also breaks notification scheduling, and destructive clock work belongs to the disposable AVD, never a fleet phone.
- The AVD as crossing witness: the e2e rules name it smoke-only, never a witness.
- Fixing defects inside the window: invalidates the proof; follow-up ticket.

## Steps

1. **Step 1: The API''s real expected times recorded, then the static fall-back proof closed** - code, 2 points. Deadline 23:00 BST.
2. **Step 2: iPhone XS carrying the prod build through first sync, pre-crossing readings and the midnight rollover** - device, 3 points. 23:00-00:20 BST, hard prep end 01:30.
3. **Step 3: The crossing watch: four instants transcribed (R1-R4)** - device, 3 points. 01:45-02:20. The 3T extension runs inside this step only on the lead''s handover.
4. **Step 4: Post-crossing coherence: display and the offline stored rows** - device, 3 points. 02:20-02:50 GMT.
5. **Step 5: Fajr fires on time after the crossing** - device, 3 points. Fajr-10 to Fajr+10 GMT per Step 1''s fetched value.
6. **Step 6: Findings consolidated, bells restored, every acceptance criterion answered** - docs, 1 point. After Step 5.

Total: 15 points.

Step detail:

**Step 1** (code, 2). Fetch the expected values first, key never printed:
```sh
curl -s "https://www.londonprayertimes.com/api/times?format=json&key=$(tr -d '' \n\r'' < ~/.config/athan/.api_key)&year=2026&24hours=true"
```
Transcribe into a ticket comment: the six times for 24, 25 and 26 Oct; the Extras Midnight and Last Third instants for the 24-25 night; Fajr 25 Oct in GMT (the Step 5 time-box); the expected countdown targets at R1 for both schedules. Then run `yarn test:tz`; run `yarn jest shared/__tests__/time.test.ts -t "fall" --silent` and `yarn jest shared/__tests__/notifications.test.ts -t "budget" --silent`, reading the "N passed" lines per the jest gotcha. Write the three gap tests with the clock mocked and the store seeded from the fetched real 24-26 Oct rows: (a) `getTodayDateString` at 2026-10-25T00:30:00Z (first 01:xx pass) and 2026-10-25T01:30:00Z (second pass) both return ''2026-10-25''; (b) `collectCandidateRows` / `firstStillDueListDayForPrayer` with now = 2026-10-25T01:30:00Z: a yesterday night row whose instant passed is not armed, every armed row is ordered by UTC instant; (c) `getSecondsRemaining` either side of 2026-10-25T01:00:00Z decreases one second per real second and never returns 0 before the target. Each gap test is proven able to fail by a mutation pass: flip the guarded logic it pins, watch it fail, revert, and record the failing run in the ticket. `yarn validate` green. No production code changes.

**Step 2** (device, 3). Version bump per the decision above. Build the iOS prod Release per the atlas "Device build" and "Device build-only" rows: prebuild, `EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=prod`, `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_KEY` from the key file into the process env only, `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` inline, xcodebuild for a device artifact, `xcrun devicectl device install app` on `IPHONE_UDID`. The iOS build precedes any 3T build tonight (`build-prod.zsh` refuses to start beside an xcodebuild, and the slot rule is never two at once). Prepare the tap driver per the atlas Driver row before the first read. Launch once, compare the screen against Step 1''s transcription to prove real times served and stored, leave it foregrounded to finish sync and arming. Read the bell state with the bells sheet; enable both schedules'' at-time athans when off, prior state recorded; relaunch once after any change. Pre-crossing readings 23:45-23:59 BST: both schedules'' full lists and day labels, both countdown targets, the home screen (recording whether a widget sits on it), the overlay. Midnight rollover: reads at 23:58 and 00:03 BST transcribing the day label move Sat 24 to Sun 25 on both schedules, the Standard countdown target moving to Fajr, the lists swapping days. All reads are screenshots; the atlas''s traps section governs.

**Step 3** (device, 3). Session opens 01:45, app foregrounded on the Standard page. At R1, R2 (bracketed), R3, R4 transcribe from screenshots: wall clock and UTC; countdown target name and remaining on both schedules (Standard''s displayed remaining drops five minutes per interval; Extras flips Last Third to Suhoor when its instant passes); day label on both schedules; both schedules'' row lists (the 25 Oct Extras list carries the night''s Last Third row at R1 by design); the overlay at R1 and R4; the home screen at R3 when Step 2 found a widget on it; every notification that fires in the window, transcribed live from its banner (the Last Third row may fire near R2 when armed). The phone is locked once after R4 and the lock-screen entries transcribed. Comment the transcription on the ticket before the session ends. 3T extension, only on the lead''s handover before 23:45, sequenced after the iOS build: `$HOME/athan-gitree/bin/build-prod.zsh <ref> <out.apk>`, install on `3T_SERIAL`, assert User 0 alone per the repo command, read `e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md` first, then the same four instants from the 3T screen plus `yarn check:device 3T_SERIAL "$APP_ID" <expected-times.json>`: the R1 dump is transcribed raw and judged against nothing (dumpsys prints future triggers in the device''s current offset, so BST-hour dumps mislabel GMT triggers by an hour), the post-crossing dump is judged against Step 1''s transcription.

**Step 4** (device, 3). Foreground the app: day label Sun 25 Oct on both schedules, lists equal to Step 1''s transcription, countdown targeting the day''s next prayer. Airplane mode on, relaunch: the stored rows alone serve the same day offline (the offline invariant is the stored-rows proof on iOS), lists identical to the online read; airplane off after. Transcribe the day''s remaining prayers displaying. Transcribe the 3T''s post-crossing alarm dump when the extension ran. The bell state stays as Step 2 left it.

**Step 5** (device, 3). From Fajr-10 to Fajr+10 GMT (Step 1''s value). Lock the phone with the side button (the XS never auto-locks while tethered; manual lock works), the app foregrounded underneath the lock. Transcribe the Fajr athan notification and its lock-screen timestamp, compared against the API''s Fajr. Unlock, foreground, transcribe the countdown target advancing past Fajr. This step is the fire-on-time proof; when nothing fires, transcribe the phone''s notification settings state for the app and record the criterion unproven on iOS, with the 3T alarm dump as the fallback evidence when the extension ran.

**Step 6** (docs, 1). Restore the bell state changed in Step 2, relaunch once, and transcribe the screen read that confirms the restore. One comment per acceptance criterion naming its evidence: suite output lines, the Step 1 transcription, the rollover, R1-R4, the post reads, the Fajr fire. Verdict per criterion; every defect named with its follow-up ticket reference. `yarn validate` re-run when anything changed after Step 1.

## Risks

- The iOS build overruns 01:30: the crossing is then watched on whatever prod build the XS already carries, its build identity recorded from Settings; when the installed build is mock or unknown, the live criteria are recorded partial and the static proof carries the ticket. No clock is ever set by hand.
- A gap test exposes a real defect: recorded, follow-up ticket, no fix inside the window.
- Lane 2 contention on the Mac or the 3T: the optional path does not run; the iPhone path never waits on it.
- The XS arrives with a stale dev-cache: a previous mock build''s rows live in `athan-storage-dev` and are never read by a prod build; the Step 2 screen comparison proves the prod store served real values.
- The Last Third notification is not armed (bell off before Step 2, or the budget spent elsewhere): the fire evidence rests on Step 5''s Fajr.
- A reading is missed at an instant: the screenshot timestamps and the ticket comment carry what was caught; the window is not extended past 02:20.

## Proof

- Static suites on the tip: `yarn test:tz` green; `yarn jest shared/__tests__/time.test.ts -t "fall" --silent` and the notifications budget filter each report "N passed" with N > 0; the three gap tests land with their mutation-pass failing runs and their green runs in the ticket.
- Before the crossing: the Step 1 curl transcription equals the XS screen read in Step 2 (both schedules, both countdowns, day labels, bell state); the build report lines and the install output recorded.
- Through the crossing: the Step 3 comment carries four timestamped reading sets; Standard''s displayed remaining drops five minutes per five real minutes across R1-R2 and R2-R3 with target and day fixed; identical day label and list content across the two 01:xx passes; the Extras flip to Suhoor at its instant; every firing notification transcribed from its banner and the lock screen.
- After the crossing: the Step 4 comment carries the online read and the airplane-mode relaunch read (the stored rows serving the day offline), and the remaining prayers; the 3T post-crossing alarm dump shows every remaining prayer armed at its true local time when the extension ran.
- Fire on time: the Step 5 comment carries the Fajr notification transcript against the API''s Fajr value.
- Gates: `yarn validate` green in Step 1 and re-run in Step 6; all findings recorded on this ticket as they happen.

## Findings answered (grill, 2026-10-24)

1. Bell restore disarms Step 5''s Fajr: fixed - the restore moved to Step 6, after the fire.
2. No tap driver named: fixed - the atlas Driver route (agent-device CLI, prepared iOS runner, runner apps uninstalled at the night''s end) is a recorded decision and Step 2 prepares it before the first read.
3. Bell toggle re-arm uncertainty: fixed - one relaunch after any bell change before 01:30; the sheet-dismiss commit and the launch listener together make the armed state certain.
4. "Armed alarms recorded" has no iOS read: fixed - the decision names the iOS substitute (bell-state screenshots plus the fires) and assigns the alarm dump to the 3T extension; the ticket''s acceptance line now says the same.
5. "Nothing re-fetches wrongly" unobservable on prod: fixed - the criterion now reads as the observable pair: the reopen shows the API''s own 25 Oct values, and the airplane-mode relaunch serves the day from stored rows alone.
6. The 300-second delta unscoped: fixed - scoped to Standard as an exact five-minute displayed drop per interval; the Extras Last Third to Suhoor flip is its own expected reading.
7. "Red first" against green-on-arrival pins: fixed - each gap test carries a mutation pass (flip the guarded logic, watch it fail, revert) recorded in the ticket.
8. Test (b) needed the real rows first: fixed - Step 1 now fetches and transcribes the API values before writing the gap tests, which seed from them.
9. The R1 3T dump false-fails on the BST offset: fixed - R1 transcribed raw and judged against nothing; expected times judged only on the post-crossing dump.
10. Lock-screen read moments and the banned home gesture: fixed - banners live in the window, one lock after R4 for the lock-screen entries, and "backgrounded" means locked with the app foregrounded.
11. The Last Third row''s list placement: fixed - the design section and Step 3 name it as the 25 Oct Extras list''s row at R1, the expected state.
12. The literal UDID and the public board snapshot: fixed - the doc now carries `IPHONE_UDID` only.
13. Widget presence never established: fixed - Step 2''s home-screen read records which case holds, fixing R3''s reading set.
14. The Ticket number field: fixed on the ticket (set to 337), matching the convention T-322 carries.
