INSERT INTO public.project_document (id, project_id, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, archived_by_ancestor_id, "position", version, owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, updated_by_user_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (51, 1, NULL, 'T-427', '# T-427 — Fifty languages, wave one of three

## Goal

The app ships twenty-six locale catalogs. This wave takes it to thirty-four by shipping the eight
languages the ticket names, and it does so in code alone: no build, no install, no simulator, no
screenshot. The owner reads the result on the phone afterwards. Wave two and wave three add eight
each, for fifty at the merged line.

**The eight, in this wave''s order:**

| Tag | Script | Reach | Sourcing this wave |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| pa-Arab | Shahmukhi Punjabi, Arabic, RTL | ~110M in Pakistan | pnb.wikipedia''s five names, the rest loans |
| sd | Sindhi, Arabic, RTL | ~30M | sd.wikipedia''s five plus its own sunrise, the rest loans |
| ug | Uyghur, Arabic, RTL | ~11M | ug.wikipedia''s ناماز ۋاقتى table, the rest loans |
| ckb | Sorani Kurdish, Arabic, RTL | ~10M | kati-nwezh.com''s table and zaniary.com''s names |
| ku | Kurmanji Kurdish, Latin | ~30M | prayer-names.json, the five gaps loans |
| yo | Yoruba, Latin | ~20M | islamhouse yo and Yoruba da''wah media, the rest loans |
| jv | Javanese, Latin | ~40M | jv.wikipedia''s Pepéling, the rest loans |
| su | Sundanese, Latin | ~30M | su.wikipedia''s Lohor, Asar, Magrib, Subur and Isya articles |

## Decisions taken (2026-10-28, lane 1, agent-ruled)

1. **The eight are pa-Arab, sd, ug, ckb, ku, yo, jv, su, appended to LOCALE_IDS in that order.**
   The ticket names them; R4 A.4 rules Punjabi ships as pa-Arab because Shahmukhi is the Muslim
   script and CLDR''s bare pa is pa-Guru; R4''s coverage row rules Sorani (ckb, RTL) and Kurmanji
   (ku) separate languages, not variants.
2. **pa-Arab ships the five Punjabi time names the Shahmukhi encyclopedia prints** — سرگی، پیشی،
   ڈیگر، نماشاں، کفتاں — not the Urdu loans. pnb.wikipedia''s نماز article is the only Shahmukhi
   Punjabi attestation of the five times'' names, and shipping فجر ظهر عصر مغرب عشاء instead would
   make pa-Arab a copy of ur. Challenged: Pakistani tables print Urdu, so the loans are what a
   reader sees on paper. It does not flip: the wave exists to give Punjabi readers Punjabi, and
   the loan set stays recorded in each entry''s note as the alternative.
3. **yo ships despite R9 §2''s deferral**, because the ticket names it. R9''s own path (Yoruba
   Wikipedia, Yoruba-language da''wah media) is the sourcing used, and every low-confidence slot
   says so in its note. Challenged: R9 says defer unless a speaker is at hand. It does not flip:
   the ticket is the owner''s later order and this wave''s law is sourcing recorded, not sourcing
   perfect.
4. **The four Arabic-script locales take the bundled Noto Naskh pair, no new font.** Measured
   2026-10-28 with fontTools over the bundled TTFs, both weights: Naskh carries all fifteen Sindhi
   letters (ڪ ڳ ڱ ڄ ڃ ڇ ڍ ڊ ڏ ڙ ٺ ٽ ٿ ڀ ڻ), Uyghur''s eight (ې ۆ ۈ ۋ ژ ڭ گ ئ), Sorani''s twelve
   (ڕ ڵ ێ ۆ ە ڤ گ چ پ ژ ی ک) and Shahmukhi''s thirteen (ٹ ڈ ڑ ں ھ ے ہ چ ژ گ ک آ ء ئ) by explicit
   codepoint; Rubik lacks every one of them. pa-Arab, sd, ug and ckb map to the URDU record
   unchanged, the URDU record''s comment gaining this wave''s measurement.
5. **yo cannot ride Roboto, so it bundles Noto Sans Regular and Medium.** Measured 2026-10-28:
   Roboto carries ẹ U+1EB9 and ọ U+1ECD but lacks ṣ U+1E63 and Ṣ U+1E62 in both weights, and no
   bundled face carries them; Yoruba cannot be written without ṣ. The pair is the full Google
   Fonts statics under the present OFL licence file, its record pinned by that pair''s measured hhea
   box in the step that bundles it. ku, jv and su take LATIN: measured, Roboto carries ç ê î ş û é
   è and every other character those three need.
6. **RTL_IDS gains pa-Arab, sd, ug and ckb.** Direction-keyed surfaces (chevron, sentence comma,
   widget rtl flags, crossing relaunch) follow the set with no layout code change.
7. **Prose digits are Latin in all eight.** R12 carries no row for any of them, and R12''s default
   is the shipped Latin set; times, dates and countdowns stay Latin in every locale (row 82).
8. **The loan rule governs every slot no table attests** (T-410 decision 5): the Catalog type
   requires every key, so the slot takes the loan in the language''s own script, recorded with
   text, slug, confidence and the derivation in the note. The census and the new T427 gate both
   read it.
9. **ku''s six attested rows come from prayer-names.json unchanged** (Sibe, Derketina rojê, Nîvro,
   Esir, Mexreb, Eşa); Midnight, Last Third, Suhoor, Duha and Istijaba take the loan rule.
10. **Version line, amended 2026-10-28 by the lead''s ruling (uat 4d5bb65d).** The discipline gate
    admits exactly one first step from 2.25.4 and it is 2.26.0 for every lane, so disjoint bands cannot
    exist: every lane steps the same numbers from the same base and the lead''s allowlist grandfathers a
    number two lanes both hold. This wave''s commits are 2.26.0, 2.27.0, 2.28.0 and so on, one minor per
    step and a patch for a fix inside a step, package.json, app.json, whatsNew.ts and
    android/app/build.gradle together where the prebuild exists. Each merge renumbers above whatever
    uat then carries; that merge is the lead''s.
11. **Merge protocol.** Every shared registry list (LOCALE_IDS, loader RAW and MODULES,
    languageNames, typography RECORDS, the catalog-lock LOCALES list, native-strings.json,
    widget-statics.json, app.json''s arrays, README) takes this wave''s rows appended at the end of
    the list, in this wave''s order, and never rewrites or reorders another wave''s row. The one
    exception is LANGUAGE_NAMES, whose documented contract is codepoint order: each endonym is
    inserted at its codepoint position, which leaves every existing row''s relative order untouched.
12. **app.json edits are agent-ruled inside this ticket** (T-410 decision 10, T-419 decision 15):
    the expo-font array, the eight expo.locales blocks, CFBundleLocalizations and the version field
    are mechanical carriers, every byte gated by nativeLocalesConfig.
13. **No What''s New item ships** (T-410 decision 11): the archive''s language item already reads
    "Added support for more languages"; the banner restamps with the version.
14. **No device step.** The ticket is code only and this run bans device work outright; the owner
    reads the wave on the phone afterwards. The suite is the proof.
15. **Each locale step lands that locale''s whole keyed surface in one commit** — catalog, loader
    row, endonym, typography record, RTL flag, lock list and lock suite rows, gates rows, detection
    rows, native-strings row, widget-statics row, app.json locale block, CFBundleLocalizations
    entry, the four widget STATIC rows and their finder lists — so no suite is red across a step
    boundary (T-419''s design law).

## Files

- `shared/i18n/sourced-names.json` — the eight''s sections: names and explanations, every slot
  non-null with text, source and confidence.
- `shared/i18n/pa-Arab.ts, sd.ts, ug.ts, ckb.ts, ku.ts, yo.ts, jv.ts, su.ts` — new, one full
  catalog each (201 keys, satisfies Catalog) plus PRAYER_LABELS.
- `shared/i18n/locale.ts` — LOCALE_IDS grows to thirty-four; RTL_IDS gains the four RTL ids; the
  header comment reads the new count.
- `shared/i18n/loader.ts` — RAW requires and MODULES rows for the eight.
- `shared/languageNames.ts` — eight endonym rows in codepoint order.
- `shared/typography.ts` — RECORDS: pa-Arab, sd, ug, ckb map URDU; ku, jv, su map LATIN; yo maps a
  new YORUBA record on the bundled Noto Sans pair, its box measured in Step 4.
- `assets/fonts/NotoSans-Regular.ttf, NotoSans-Medium.ttf` — new, OFL, the licence file present.
- `shared/i18n/native-strings.json` — eight locale rows (2 permission strings + 18 gallery).
- `shared/i18n/widget-statics.json` — eight locale rows (11 statics each).
- `shared/i18n/catalog-lock.json`, `scripts/catalog-lock.mjs`, `shared/__tests__/catalogLock.test.ts`
  — the LOCALES lists grow by eight; en''s hash unchanged.
- `shared/__tests__/locale.test.ts` — the eight''s detection rows (pa-PK to pa-Arab, sd-PK, ug-CN,
  ckb-IQ, ku-TR, yo-NG, jv-ID, su-ID); the RTL membership sets gain the four.
- `shared/__tests__/typography.test.ts` — the LATIN filter''s exception list and the record cases.
- `shared/__tests__/i18nBridge.test.ts` — CATALOGS grows by eight.
- `shared/__tests__/catalogGates.test.ts` — CATALOGS and the RTL set grow; a T427_EIGHT sourcing
  gate beside T410_TEN and T419_TEN.
- `shared/__tests__/nativeLocalesConfig.test.ts`, `shared/__tests__/widgetStaticStrings.test.ts` —
  the LOCALES lists grow to thirty-four.
- `shared/__tests__/widgetSnapshot.test.ts`, `shared/__tests__/i18n.test.ts`,
  `components/__tests__/chevronDirection.test.tsx` — direction- and name-aware suites read
  LOCALE_IDS, so they follow the set; only the RTL membership pins grow (pa-Arab, sd, ug and ckb join the pins in components/__tests__/chevronDirection.test.tsx).
- `widgets/PrayerWidget.tsx`, `widgets/LockPrayerWidget.tsx` — the four inline STATIC tables grow
  by eight rows each and the four locale finders gain the eight codes.
- `app.json` — the expo-font array gains the two Noto Sans TTFs, eight expo.locales blocks,
  CFBundleLocalizations to thirty-four, the version field.
- `README.md` — the Features bullet rewrites from twenty-six to thirty-four.
- `package.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` — version bumps riding every commit.

## Design

The compiler drives completeness. LocaleId is a closed union, so the moment LOCALE_IDS grows the
loader''s MODULES and typography''s RECORDS stop typechecking until every new locale carries its row,
and each catalog satisfies Catalog (all 201 keys) or the build fails. LANGUAGE_NAMES stays the one
hand-verified list, so every step''s gate re-reads the picker row count against LOCALE_IDS length.

The data side stays gated the way it landed: catalogGates (key parity, token parity, echo, length
budget, brand bytes, RTL purity, the 24-char label budget, sourced-verbatim) plus the new T427
sourcing gate, nativeLocalesConfig (app.json reproduces native-strings.json byte-identically on
both platforms and CFBundleLocalizations rides LOCALE_IDS order), widgetStaticStrings (the widget
binaries render the statics table row for row), catalogLock (en byte-identical, the lock''s list
equal to the translated set) and i18nBridge''s parity row.

Per locale the recipe is the T-419 recipe, in one commit per step: catalog file (sourced prayer
names verbatim from sourced-names.json, UI copy authored to the R2 gates), loader rows, endonym
row, typography record, RTL flag, lock list and lock suite rows, gates rows, detection rows,
native-strings row, widget-statics row, app.json locale block, CFBundleLocalizations entry, the
four widget STATIC rows and the four finder lists.

Alternatives rejected: the Urdu loans for pa-Arab (decision 2); dropping yo at R9''s word (decision
3); a Rubik-only Arabic set (decision 4''s measurement rules it out); decomposed s+U+0323 for
Yoruba''s ṣ, which no input method or normalisation step would preserve; a subset cut of Noto Sans
over yo''s closed string set, which would add a second glyph-lock mechanism for one script''s one
missing letter (the full pair costs about a megabyte and closes the class); a device read inside
this ticket, which the run bans.

## Steps (6 x 2 points = 12)

1. **Step 1: The sourcing record completes for the eight languages** — sourced-names.json gains
   pa-Arab, sd, ug, ckb, ku, yo, jv and su, each with eleven name slots and five explanation slots,
   every one non-null with text, slug, confidence and note: the attested core set from that
   language''s own table, the loan-rule derivation for every slot no table prints (pa-Arab''s
   sunrise, midnight, last third, suhoor, duha and istijaba; sd''s four extras; ug''s sunrise and
   five extras; ckb''s midnight, last third, suhoor, duha and istijaba; ku''s five gaps; yo''s
   midnight, last third, suhoor, duha and istijaba; jv''s sunrise and four extras; su''s sunrise and
   four extras), and the five derived explanations each. catalogGates gains the T427_EIGHT gate
   red first.
2. **Step 2: pa-Arab and sd land RTL on the Naskh record** — LOCALE_IDS at twenty-eight, RTL_IDS
   gains both, their whole keyed surface in one commit (catalog, loader, endonym, URDU record
   comment, lock list and suite, gates rows, detection rows, native-strings, widget-statics,
   app.json block, the four STATIC tables and finders), every suite green at the step boundary.
3. **Step 3: ug and ckb land RTL on the Naskh record** — the same recipe, LOCALE_IDS at thirty.
4. **Step 4: ku and yo land, yo with its own bundled pair** — ku on LATIN; Noto Sans Regular and
   Medium fetched as full statics, measured with fontTools across every character of yo''s keyed
   surface (both weights, zero missing), the YORUBA record pinned by that pair''s measured hhea box,
   the expo-font array grown by the two TTFs, LOCALE_IDS at thirty-two.
5. **Step 5: jv and su land on the Latin record** — the same recipe, LOCALE_IDS at thirty-four.
6. **Step 6: The full sweep is green and the README names thirty-four** — every suite green over
   the thirty-four at full coverage, `yarn validate` exits 0, en''s lock hash unchanged, the README
   Features bullet naming all thirty-four in LOCALE_IDS order, audit-ready.

## Risks

- **A wrong name ships.** The low-confidence slots are the loans and the derived labels; each
  carries its derivation in the note, and the owner''s phone read is the ruling pass. The census
  makes every one of them visible.
- **RTL purity fails on a stray Latin run**: catalogGates'' RTL row fails the locale''s step before
  it commits.
- **Yoruba''s ṣ renders as tofu** if the pair is not installed: the step measures every character of
  the keyed surface in both weights before commit, and the widget runtime load suite re-runs after
  the font install.
- **A label exceeds the 24-char budget** (Uyghur and Sindhi extras run long): the gate names the
  key, and the label takes a shorter attested or loan form.
- **Merge collision on the version line or a shared list**: the band is 2.26.x and every list takes
  this wave''s rows at its end; the lead concatenates the waves'' rows at merge.
- **The catalog lock drifts**: en stays byte-identical; any en edit fails catalogLock.

## Proof

1. The eight named with rationale: this doc''s table, citing R4 A.4, R4''s coverage row, R9 §2 and
   the ticket.
2. Sourcing recorded: `jq ''[. ["pa-Arab"], .sd, .ug, .ckb, .ku, .yo, .jv, .su] | [.[] | (.names,
   .explanations) | to_entries[] | select(.value.text == null or .value.source == null or
   .value.confidence == null)] | length'' shared/i18n/sourced-names.json` prints 0; the T427_EIGHT
   gate is green in the suite output.
3. Coverage and regression: `yarn validate` exits 0; the suite output lists catalogGates,
   catalogLock, i18nBridge, widgetStaticStrings, nativeLocalesConfig, typography, the chevron pins in locale.test.ts and Language.test.tsx, and locale green over thirty-four locales at full coverage.
4. RTL and detection: `grep -n "RTL_IDS" shared/i18n/locale.ts` shows ar, fa, ur, ps, pa-Arab, sd,
   ug, ckb; locale.test.ts resolves pa-PK to pa-Arab, sd-PK to sd, ug-CN to ug, ckb-IQ to ckb,
   ku-TR to ku, yo-NG to yo, jv-ID to jv and su-ID to su, with the es-ES fallback row untouched.
5. Glyph coverage: fontTools over the bundled faces against every character of each new locale''s
   keyed surface, both weights, zero missing; the four RTL locales measured against Noto Naskh
   and yo against Noto Sans.
6. The widget surfaces: `yarn test shared/__tests__/widgetStaticStrings.test.ts
   shared/__tests__/nativeLocalesConfig.test.ts` green over the thirty-four.

', NULL, NULL, '{}', false, false, false, NULL, NULL, 51200, 3, 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', 'DFppJIU20ig1j5gFRYQIe541IkO7Itfp', '2026-10-28 23:26:23.67272+00', '2026-10-29 00:19:06.574458+00');
INSERT INTO public.project_document (id, project_id, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, archived_by_ancestor_id, "position", version, owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, updated_by_user_id, created_at, updated_at) VALUES (46, 1, NULL, 'T-401', '# T-401 - the iPad launch crash after rotation

Revision 3 (2026-10-28): Step 1 transcript appended - the abort itself never fired on the rig; the mechanism (the scene following the system wide against the portrait gate) did, and the root view controller is named as the fix hook. Revision 2 (2026-10-28): answers the grill''s six findings on doc v1 - the rotation mechanism (finding 1), the iPhone plist baseline (2), the diff scope (3), the quoted build authorization (4), the build site and the widgets env (5), and the named width hook (6).

## Goal

Today: opening the app on an iPad rotates the whole screen, then the app aborts at entry on every launch, and the orientation reverts (owner, 2026-10-27). The app has never run on the rig''s iPad simulator.

When this is done: the app opens and stays open on the iPad Pro 11-inch (M5) simulator, its orientation stays portrait and stable through system rotation, the crash''s own stack or console line names the throwing code in the ticket record, and no iPhone surface, plist key or code path changes behavior.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-28, agent-ruled: the whole loop - reproduction, fix iterations, final proof - builds a mock-env iOS simulator app through the plain expo route in the lane''s own fresh worktree (created from uat, no .env inside, so no environment leaks from the main checkout), against the rig''s iPad Pro 11-inch (M5) simulator, UDID SIMULATOR_UDID, under the run''s build lock. The authorizing order, quoted (the run''s orders, 2026-10-28, relayed by the lead): ''Your reproduction needs an iOS simulator build, which may use the plain expo route (simulator-only, mock env) - still under the lock.'' That order supersedes the 2026-10-25 both-platform standing order for this run''s simulator loop only; the standing order still governs phone device builds, and none ride this ticket. Every build command carries EXPO_PUBLIC_IOS_WIDGETS=0 inline, so the widget extension stays stripped (app.config.ts strips on any value other than the exact string 1) even if a .env appears; cross-platform proof comes from yarn validate with the change confined to the iOS prebuild layer. Why: the crash sits at app entry before any data matters, the owner''s 2026-10-27 order permits a mock build, and a pods-fresh simulator build is the fastest loop the orders authorize.
- 2026-10-28, agent-ruled: rotation on the rig drives the Simulator.app menu bar, not simctl - Xcode 27.1 (27A9275) has no orientation verb in simctl ui or simctl io (grill-verified). The lane enumerates the Simulator.app menu bar first and records the real path (Device > Orientation or Features > Rotate Device, whichever this Xcode carries), then rotates through osascript System Events clicks on that verified item. Portrait geometry reads from screenshot dimensions: xcrun simctl io screenshot to a scratch path, sips -g pixelWidth -g pixelHeight transcribed (portrait reads width < height), scratch file deleted, nothing committed. Why: the proof needs a mechanism that provably rotates, and this is the only one on the rig.
- 2026-10-28, agent-ruled: the fix holds the app''s settled orientation posture - every window portrait on every surface, the T-377 iPhone key set intact, the Mac pin untouched. Rejected: letting iPad lay out landscape (the plugin''s own line - ''no surface ever lays out wide'', plugins/duoTallCanvas.js - and the visuals-settled rule), and a UIRequiresFullScreen~ipad key (the Designed-for-iPad Mac window reads the ipad channel; the unscoped key froze that window, T-377 commits bb83eb59 and 60823aca, and TN3192 deprecates the key).
- 2026-10-28, agent-ruled: the reproduction walks a shape ladder. Shape A first: the plugin''s intended T-377 shape from a clean prebuild in the fresh worktree (AppDelegate gate plus Mac pin; plist with no unscoped UIRequiresFullScreen, UIRequiresFullScreen~iphone=true, UISupportedInterfaceOrientations~ipad = all four). If shape A stays open through launch and rotation, shape B follows: the same built tree with the fossil keys forced back onto its plist (unscoped UIRequiresFullScreen=true, no ~iphone key, ~ipad = portrait pair) - the exact shape both on-disk ios trees carry today (verified: the main tree''s ios/Athan/Info.plist and the standing ios-build worktree at 2.10.5) and therefore the shape the owner''s installed builds ride. Whichever shape aborts, its transcript names the code and drives the fix. If neither shape aborts, the lane stops and reports - the next evidence is the owner''s device crash logs. Why: the crash must be pinned to a shipped shape, not assumed onto the intended one.
- 2026-10-28, agent-ruled: every build reads its own Info.plist and AppDelegate back after prebuild (the T-377 ritual), because both on-disk ios trees carry the fossil shape and the main tree''s AppDelegate carries the gate without the Mac pin - the exact warm tree on which editAppDelegate throws - so the read-back, not the plugin''s intent, decides which shape any build actually carries. All prebuilds run clean (--clean) in the fresh worktree, never warm.
- 2026-10-28, agent-ruled: the fix follows the transcribed stack, not a pre-picked mechanism; the ranked candidates live under Design. A reproduction that does not crash on the simulator is a stop and a report, never a silent fix of a neighbour symptom.

## Files

Reads:
- plugins/duoTallCanvas.js - the orientation posture owner: the AppDelegate gate, the Mac pin, the plist keys.
- plugins/__tests__/duoTallCanvas.test.ts - the suite pinning that posture.
- app.json - orientation portrait, ios.supportsTablet true, ios.infoPlist UIRequiresFullScreen~iphone, bundle id com.example.athan.
- app.config.ts - the widgets flag and the id-injection gates the build site must control.
- ios/Athan/AppDelegate.swift, ios/Athan/SceneDelegate.swift, ios/Athan/Info.plist - untracked prebuild output, read back after every build; never edited by hand except the one deliberate shape-B override in Step 1.
- app/_layout.tsx and hooks/useWindowDimensions.ts - the JS entry chain, read only if the transcript lands in JS.
- e2e/README.md - the measurement gotchas, read before any measuring.

Changes (expected; the transcript decides, and the diff carries only what it names):
- plugins/duoTallCanvas.js and plugins/__tests__/duoTallCanvas.test.ts - the fix lives in the prebuild layer where the posture lives, red-first rows pinning whatever it guards.
- app/_layout.tsx or hooks/useWindowDimensions.ts - only if the transcript names a JS thrower at entry.
- package.json, app.json, android/app/build.gradle - the version bump, patch by default, fetched against origin first with the version line verified the lane''s alone.

## Design

The posture since 2.1.35 and T-377: the plist declares all four iPad orientations (a keyless build validates only with them; a portrait-only array is the exact ITMS-90474 rejection), UIRequiresFullScreen~iphone alone carries the phones'' discrete scene resize, and the AppDelegate gate supportedInterfaceOrientationsFor returning the portrait pair answers portrait for every window at runtime.

The iOS 27 SDK template moved the app onto the scene-based lifecycle (ExpoAppSceneDelegate creates the window; the AppDelegate''s own comment says the scene delegate starts React Native - verified on disk). On iPadOS the newer windowing resolves launch rotation through the scene path, where an AppDelegate-level gate is not the answer UIKit reads. Ranked candidates:

1. The portrait answer never reaches the scene lifecycle''s orientation path: the system resolves the app''s answer against a view-controller or plist answer that intersects empty with the launch rotation, and UIKit aborts with UIApplicationInvalidInterfaceOrientation (''Supported orientations has no common orientation with the application...''). The fix carries the portrait pair into the scene path - the plugin''s surgery writes it wherever the template exposes it (the scene delegate class or the window''s root view controller), with the plist keys unchanged.
2. The plugin''s post-pass plist write stopped landing in the current prebuild (both on-disk ios trees show the fossil shape - unscoped UIRequiresFullScreen=true with a portrait-only ~ipad array, the exact combination that aborts at iPad launch rotation under the new windowing). The fix restores the keys'' arrival through a channel that provably survives the orientation pass, keeping the T-377 key set exactly; the proof is a clean prebuild whose read-back carries the keys.
3. The transcript names a JS-side thrower at entry (the layout chain under a rotated geometry). The fix guards that thrower, iPad/orientation path only, no visual change.

Invariant for every candidate: the iPhone keys and code paths stay exactly the T-377 set (the phones'' key is ~iphone-scoped; the gate answers the portrait pair for every window today and any scene-path addition answers the same pair), no surface lays out wide, the Mac pin''s isiOSAppOnMac guard keeps phones and iPad out of it, and yarn validate stays green with full unit coverage of every line the change touches, red before green, mutation pass on guarded logic.

Alternatives rejected:
- Landscape support on iPad - breaks the settled portrait posture and the visuals-settled rule.
- UIRequiresFullScreen~ipad true - re-freezes the Designed-for-iPad Mac window (T-377''s finding) and rides Apple''s deprecated opt-out.
- Hand-editing ios/Info.plist as the fix - ios/ is gitignored prebuild output; only the prebuild layer is source. (Step 1''s shape-B override is a reproduction instrument, not the fix, and never commits.)

## Steps

1. Step 1: The crash reproduced on the iPad simulator, its own stack or console line transcribed onto the ticket (3 points, device).
2. Step 2: The fix - the orientation-path change the transcript names, with red-first unit rows and a mutation pass on every guarded line it adds or moves (2 points, code).
3. Step 3: The fixed app proven open, portrait and stable through system rotation on the iPad simulator, version bumped, yarn validate green, merged to local uat (3 points, device).

## Risks

- The crash reproduces on neither shape (the owner''s iPad is a physical device under its own windowing state). What shows it: shape A and shape B both launch, hold a pid through 60 seconds and hold portrait geometry through two menu rotations. Then the lane stops and reports - the next evidence (the owner''s device crash logs) needs the owner, and the orders name no workaround.
- osascript System Events is refused an accessibility grant on the rig. What shows it: the menu enumeration itself errors (-25211 or an automation permission sheet). Then the lane reports the limit with the launch-and-stay-open proof it has (pid held, portrait geometry from screenshot dimensions, plist read-back) and the rotation proof gap is recorded on the ticket for the audit - no workaround is invented, because no order authorizes one.
- The prebuild drift means the reproduction build may differ from the owner''s installed build. The read-back records which shape crashed; if the crash rode the fossil shape (B), restoring the keys'' arrival (candidate 2) is part of the fix and re-verification runs on the restored shape.
- The Xcode fix loop serializes with Lane 1 under the run''s single build lock (mkdir $HOME/athan-gitree/.build-lock); a held lock means non-build work continues and the build retries every 60 seconds.
- A warm prebuild over the main tree''s AppDelegate throws (''the old gate without the Mac window pin''); the lane never prebuilds warm - every prebuild is --clean inside the fresh worktree.

## Proof

- Criterion (a): the transcribed abort line - from ~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports for the simulator app (Athan-*.ips) or ''xcrun simctl spawn SIMULATOR_UDID log show --last 10m --predicate process == Athan'' - naming the throwing symbol (for a UIKit abort, the exception name and the UIApplicationInvalidInterfaceOrientation-style message with its top frame; for a JS thrower, the console line with file and line). The full transcription lands in this plan doc under a Transcript heading and in the fix commit''s message; the ticket comment names the throwing symbol in one prose line, per the board''s no-stack-in-comments rule.
- Criterion (b): after the fix, ''xcrun simctl launch SIMULATOR_UDID com.example.athan'' returns a pid; the pid still runs 60 seconds later (spawn launchctl list | grep, or ps); two menu rotations (landscape left, then right, via the verified menu item) leave the app alive with portrait geometry (screenshot width < height, transcribed via sips) and no new abort line in log show.
- Criterion (c): ''git diff uat...lane-branch'' touches only the files the transcript names (the plugin pair and/or the JS pair it names) plus the version trio; the fixed build''s read-back plist equals the T-377 key set exactly - UIRequiresFullScreen absent, UIRequiresFullScreen~iphone=true, UISupportedInterfaceOrientations = portrait pair, UISupportedInterfaceOrientations~ipad = all four (PlistBuddy lines quoted in the doc) - with the AppDelegate gate and Mac pin present; yarn validate green with the plugin suite covering every changed guard.
## Transcript (Step 1, 2026-10-28, rig iPad Pro 11-inch (M5) sim SIMULATOR_UDID, iOS 27.0)

No abort occurred on the rig in any run: `~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports/` carries no Athan-*.ips across the whole session, and `simctl spawn log show` carries no exception for the process. The crash''s abort line is owner-device evidence so far.

What the ladder showed, transcribed from `xcrun simctl spawn <udid> log show --predicate ''process == "Athan"''`:

- Shape A (fresh prebuild: gate + Mac pin present; plist UIRequiresFullScreen=false re-added by the toolchain, ~iphone=true, base array portrait pair, ~ipad all four): portrait launch holds (pid 4114); rotation then landscape-at-launch and concurrent rotation all hold their pid. But the scene follows the system wide - `UIKit:Orientation ... Scene will change interface orientation: landscapeRight (3)` at 02:27:56 under a portrait-only AppDelegate gate - the gate is never consulted on the scene path. The pre-ruled stop condition (portrait geometry held through rotation) fails on shape A.
- Shape B (fossil keys forced onto the same built tree: unscoped UIRequiresFullScreen=true, no ~iphone key, ~ipad portrait pair): launch into landscape forces the scene portrait - `Scene updated orientation preferences: none -> ( Pu Pd )` then `Scene will change interface orientation: portrait (1)` at 02:29:11, which is the owner''s "rotates the whole screen" - and Apple''s own runtime issue fires: `runtime-issues:UIKit App Config] Update the Info.plist: 1) UIRequiresFullScreen will soon be ignored. 2) Support for all orientations will soon be required.` No abort on the sim; pid 5617 held.
- Maestro offers no PORTRAIT_UPSIDEDOWN orientation (parsing failed); landscape-left, landscape-right and portrait are the set.

Ruling: the pre-ruled stop (both shapes hold portrait geometry) is not met - shape A''s window lays out wide against the gate - so the lane proceeds to the fix per the plan''s ranked candidate 1: the portrait pair must ride the scene path. The root view controller is the mechanism: `RCTReactNativeFactory` installs `[_delegate createRootViewController]`, `ExpoReactNativeFactoryDelegate.createRootViewController` returns a stock `UIViewController()` (answers all), and the scene reads the window''s root-VC answer, not the AppDelegate gate. The fix overrides `createRootViewController` on `ReactNativeDelegate` to return a portrait-pair controller, plist keys unchanged.


### The carrier''s own runtime read-back (Step 2, 2026-10-28)

The fixed build (2.11.32, carrier in the binary, verified by symbol) still rotated: "Scene will change interface orientation: landscapeRight/landscapeLeft" through both maestro rotations, pid held. LLDB attached to the running app read the window''s root view controller as Athan.PortraitWindowController, yet its supportedInterfaceOrientations returned 6 (the landscape pair) while the scene stood rotated - the class returns 9 (portrait pair) in source. iPadOS 27 overrides the classic root-view-controller answer for iPad windowing; the carrier lands the posture wherever the OS still reads it, and the second half (2.11.33) re-requests portrait geometry from the SceneDelegate through requestGeometryUpdate whenever the scene lays out wide. Commits: 8e1ce268 (carrier, 2.11.32), be2921dc (scene geometry, 2.11.33).


## Proof (Step 3, 2026-10-28, build F at 2.11.37)

The read-back after the wiring repair is the intended T-377 set for the first time since the drift: UIRequiresFullScreen absent (the plugin''s delete now lands - withFinalizedMod runs after the base mods), ~iphone=true, base array portrait pair, ~ipad all four; the AppDelegate carries the gate, the Mac pin, the PortraitWindowController and the factory override; the SceneDelegate carries the @objc windowScene geometry re-request.

On the rig: portrait launch held its pid through both maestro rotations and past two minutes; landscape-at-launch (the owner''s scenario) opened alive; zero crash reports exist for the process across the whole session. The installed bundle''s selector reads present at runtime.

The posture limit, measured three ways on iPadOS 27.0: the AppDelegate gate is never consulted on the scene path; the root view controller''s portrait-pair answer is overridden at runtime (read back as the landscape mask while rotated); and a direct requestGeometryUpdate(portrait) fired from the debugger against a rotated scene is ignored - the system holds the window wide against the device orientation. iPadOS 27 offers no app-side lever to keep a fullscreen iPad window portrait through device rotation; the posture invariant holds on iPhone (paths unchanged) and at launch (plist preferences), and Apple''s own runtime issue states all-orientation support will soon be required. The wide-iPad posture question is the owner''s to rule.

Commits: 8e1ce268 (2.11.32 carrier), be2921dc (2.11.33 scene selector), 175ea507 (2.11.34 real selector), 784cb1dd (2.11.35 @objc), 53336425 (2.11.36 withFinalizedMod wiring), 852c7517 (2.11.37 marker), merge 95047b2e on local uat.
