INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (97, 34, 1, NULL, 'T-322', '# T-322 — A visual polish pass: the colour modal''s backdrop, the 3T''s reset ink, the header labels'' ink, the qibla sheet''s doubled instruction text, and bold platform words in Help

## Goal

Five visual defects stand on uat today: the colour modal opens with no dimming behind it, the reset control renders a black word on the 3T instead of hiding, the two header labels carry one ink in both home and overlay states, the qibla sheet''s header shows a doubled darker line while the calibration runs, and Help''s widget answer carries its platform words in the same weight as the sentence. When this ticket is done, the modal dims exactly as the other bottom sheets do, the reset hides in ink that no platform renders black, each header label carries its tuned home ink and its tuned overlay ink, the qibla header shows exactly one instruction line, and the platform words read bold in all six shipped locales. The owner reads every item on glass; the lane ships code, tests and a green `yarn validate`, nothing else.

Planned against uat f97cd7d4 (2.4.17), which carries ticket 294''s colour-carried dim whole. The ticket''s planning note named 294''s conversion as the prime suspect for the reset ink and the doubled qibla line: verified. Both defects are `color: ''transparent''` on a Text — alpha-0 ink, which Android paints black. They are the only two alpha-0 text colours left in app/ and components/.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-24 — The two Android black-ink defects are one defect class: alpha-0 text ink. The fix paints hidden text in the literal surface solid (`COLORS.surface.sheet`), the same ruling 294''s QiblaSubtitle already follows, and the text-ink sweep inside `yarn validate` is tightened to ban alpha-0 outright so the class cannot return. Why: exactly two alpha-0 sites exist in the tree and both are this ticket''s defects, so the tightened sweep reddens them and nothing else.
- 2026-10-24 — The colour modal''s backdrop is `COLORS.surface.backdrop` (#000116) composited at the 0.9 the shared `renderBackdrop` passes, pre-composited as one rgba constant because the overlay View must not dim its own children. A pinning test derives the constant from `COLORS.surface.backdrop`, so the modal and the sheets cannot drift apart. Tap-outside dismissal is unchanged: the acceptance asks for the dimming alone.
- 2026-10-24 — The header labels'' tuned inks are two new `COLORS.text` roles derived from today''s shared ink #6c79c2 (h231 s41 l59) by measured shifts: home `#7485b9` (hue to 225, toward the band behind''s #031a4c at h221; saturation to 33, the blue-grey; lightness held) and overlay `#7173bc` (hue to 238, toward the glow''s #5b1eaa at h266; saturation to 36, the greyer; lightness held). Why: the owner gave direction, not values; these are one small step from today''s ink in the named directions, and the owner''s glass read is the bar. Countdown''s label rides the `overlayProgress` it already computes; Day''s location rides the `showOverlayDate` flag its masjid already rides — no new atoms.
- 2026-10-24 — Help''s bold platform words split at render time on the pinned Latin labels (`iOS: ` / `Android: `), bolding the label run in the app''s emphasis face. The six catalogs are untouched. Why: the shipped widget copy is byte-pinned with Latin labels in every locale (owner-ruled D142.11) and hash-locked; splitting at render keeps that contract and needs no lock churn.
- 2026-10-24 — Versioning: every commit runs `git fetch origin` first and takes the next free patch number above the highest it sees (uat is 2.4.17, so 2.4.18 or higher), bumping `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` and `shared/whatsNew.ts` together. Patch class throughout: no step types its subject `feat`. No prebuild, no build, no install — the owner ordered code only.

## Files

- `shared/constants.ts` — gains `surface.backdropDim` and the two `text` roles `labelHome` and `labelOverlay`.
- `components/sheets/screens/ColorPicker.tsx` — the modal overlay''s background; the reset''s hidden ink.
- `components/sheets/screens/Qibla.tsx` — the subtitle donor''s ink.
- `components/__tests__/textInk.test.ts` — the sweep bans alpha-0 text ink.
- `components/sheets/screens/__tests__/ColorPicker.test.tsx`, `components/sheets/screens/__tests__/Qibla.test.tsx` — the new pins.
- `components/countdown/Countdown.tsx`, `components/day/Day.tsx` — the two labels'' inks.
- `hooks/useAnimation.ts` — `useDerivedColor`, the derived-ink hook the sweep''s `TEXT_INK_HOOKS` list already guards; it returns with two real consumers.
- `components/countdown/__tests__/Countdown.test.tsx`, `components/day/__tests__/DayLines.test.tsx` — the ink pins (Countdown.test.tsx:189''s `text.secondary` pin moves to `labelHome`).
- `shared/help.ts`, `shared/__tests__/help.test.ts` — the pure label splitter and its pins.
- `components/modals/Help.tsx`, `components/modals/__tests__/Help.test.tsx` — the bold render and its pins.
- Version files on every commit: `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle`, `shared/whatsNew.ts`.

## Design

**The backdrop.** The colour modal is a plain RN `Modal` whose overlay View paints `transparent`. It takes `backgroundColor: COLORS.surface.backdropDim` = `rgba(0, 1, 22, 0.9)` — the channels of `COLORS.surface.backdrop` (#000116) at the 0.9 the sheets'' shared `renderBackdrop` composites. The alpha rides the colour, never the View''s `opacity`, so the modal content above it stays opaque. The test derives the expected string from `COLORS.surface.backdrop` at build time, pinning the derivation rather than the bytes.

**The hidden inks.** The reset text hides today at `color: ''transparent''`; on Android that paints black, so the 3T shows a black reset word at default colour. The qibla subtitle''s width donor carries the same `''transparent''`. Both paint `COLORS.surface.sheet` (#0b183a) instead — the exact solid each sits on (verified: no background between either text and the sheet surface), the same rule the subtitle''s own crossfade already interpolates to. The reset stays mounted so the row holds its width, and its accessibility hiding stays as it is. The sweep''s offence condition drops its 0 carve-out on every arm (static colours, ink-hook endpoints, animated interpolations), the header comment and the roles test say alpha exactly 1, and `alphaOf`''s parser self-test stays because the parser still must read `transparent` to name it an offence.

**The label inks.** Two `COLORS.text` roles carry the tuned values. Each label keeps its static style colour at the home ink and interpolates to the overlay ink through `useDerivedColor`, a thin hook over `useDerivedProgress` + `interpolateColor` between two opaque solids — 294''s own pattern, sweep-checked at its endpoints, first frame settled because `useDerivedProgress` snaps on first evaluation. Countdown''s prayer name rides the `overlayProgress` its digits already ride; Day''s location rides a derived progress on `showOverlayDate` at `ANIMATION.duration`, the same flag and duration its masjid fade rides. The date line, the countdown digits and everything else keep their inks.

**The bold words.** `splitPlatformLine` in `shared/help.ts` matches a line against `/^(iOS|Android): /` and returns the label run and the remainder, or null. Help''s answer Text renders each line with the label run wrapped in a nested Text carrying `ty.familyMedium` — the emphasis face the question rows already carry, per locale. The six catalogs, the lock file and the byte-pinned copy tests are untouched; the splitter is pinned against every locale''s real catalog string.

**Alternatives rejected.** Hiding the reset by unmounting it: the row''s right side re-layouts when a colour is picked, a pixel change the owner has not ordered. Hiding by wrapper View opacity: it paints text through opacity, the exact thing 294''s sweep exists to stop. Deriving the labels'' overlay ink from the glow at runtime: the tune is a fixed pair of ruled constants, not a computation, so it stays testable as bytes. Stripping the platform prefixes out of the six catalogs and bolding code-supplied words: it fights the owner-ruled Latin-label copy contract and churns the hash lock for no gain.

## Steps

1. **Step 1: the colour modal carries the sheets'' dimming backdrop** (2 points). `surface.backdropDim` lands in `shared/constants.ts`; `ColorPicker.tsx`''s `modalOverlay` paints it; `ColorPicker.test.tsx` pins the overlay colour and its derivation from `COLORS.surface.backdrop` at 0.9, red first.
2. **Step 2: alpha-0 text ink leaves the tree** (2 points). The sweep bans every alpha that is not 1 across its arms and its roles test; watched red, it names exactly the reset''s `''transparent''` and the donor''s `''transparent''`; both paint `COLORS.surface.sheet`; `ColorPicker.test.tsx` pins the reset''s colour per state (sheet solid at default, `#5b77a4` shown, `#1f3055` custom under a hidden bar) and `Qibla.test.tsx` pins the donor''s ink; sweep green.
3. **Step 3: the header labels take their tuned home and overlay inks** (2 points). `text.labelHome` `#7485b9` and `text.labelOverlay` `#7173bc` land; `useDerivedColor` returns to `hooks/useAnimation.ts` with the two consumers; `Countdown.tsx` and `Day.tsx` carry it; the countdown and Day suites pin the home colour and the home-to-overlay interpolation endpoints, red first.
4. **Step 4: Help''s platform words read bold in every shipped language** (2 points). `splitPlatformLine` lands in `shared/help.ts`; `Help.tsx` bolds the label run; `help.test.ts` pins the split over all six locales'' widget answers and the null path on other answers; `Help.test.tsx` pins the emphasis face on the label runs and the regular face on the sentences, red first.

Every step ends with `yarn validate` green and its own version bump. No step drives a phone, builds, installs or reads a screenshot: the owner tests every visual item on glass.

## Risks

- The tuned inks are derived, not owner-seen. They sit one measured step from today''s ink in the directions the owner named; if the glass read disagrees, a follow-up tune re-rules the two constants and nothing else moves.
- The hidden-ink-as-surface-solid rule holds while the surface behind each text is exactly `COLORS.surface.sheet`. Verified today for both sites; a future card background behind either row would need the constant re-ruled, which the per-site colour pins would surface.
- The tightened sweep could name a file this plan did not read. The sweep runs inside `yarn validate` at Step 2''s gate, so any surprise stops that step, not a later one.
- Two more animated styles run on the UI thread (the labels). The qibla subtitle already runs the same shape; nothing measurable is expected.

## Proof

- Colour modal backdrop: `ColorPicker.test.tsx` asserts the modal root''s overlay paints `COLORS.surface.backdropDim` and that the constant equals `COLORS.surface.backdrop`''s channels at 0.9. `yarn validate` green. The owner''s glass read closes it.
- Reset ink: `ColorPicker.test.tsx` asserts the reset text''s colour per state, with `COLORS.surface.sheet` at default and never `''transparent''` in any state; the tightened sweep refuses any alpha-0 text colour anywhere in app/ and components/. The owner''s glass read on the 3T closes it.
- Header labels: `Countdown.test.tsx` and `DayLines.test.tsx` pin `labelHome` at rest and the interpolation endpoints `labelHome` to `labelOverlay` on the overlay flag. The owner''s glass read closes both states.
- Qibla doubled line: `Qibla.test.tsx` pins the donor''s ink at `COLORS.surface.sheet`; the existing suite already pins the two-line crossfade geometry and inks; the sweep bans the alpha-0 class. The owner''s glass read closes it.
- Help bold: `help.test.ts` pins `splitPlatformLine` over each of the six locales'' `help.a.widgets` lines; `Help.test.tsx` pins the medium family on the label runs and the regular family on the sentences. The owner''s glass read closes it.
- Whole ticket: `yarn validate` green after every step, each commit carrying its fetched-next version bump across `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` and `shared/whatsNew.ts`.
