## Design

Measurement first, conclusion second. The owner''s suspicion (ticket 294''s colour conversion era) is a hypothesis; the bisect owns the truth. The 3T (2017, SD820) is the floor device and the only measurement witness. The XS (2018, A12) is the control that must not move. The AVD is smoke-only and never a witness.

Hypotheses, named to be tested, not concluded:
- H1 (294, e3d3bf9d) the per-row veiled ink. Each row element carries useDerivedVeiledColor: two useDerivedProgress values plus an animated style whose worklet runs a nested interpolateColor (an inner interpolation between two hex strings inside an outer one) every frame, every element. An overlay open on the Standard list runs this on every hidden row''s name, digits and colon (five rows), plus the ago badge''s two hooks and the bell''s fill: dozens of concurrent per-frame colour interpolations on the UI thread. The XS absorbs that work; an SD820 may not.
- H2 (294, e3d3bf9d and b234c995) the hold-then-hide timers. Each hidden row''s hiddenSettled setTimeout fires ANIMATION_DURATION after the open and commits display:none through a JS re-render, landing inside the overlay entrance''s own frames; the ago badge and the info box add their own timers.
- H3 (294, 4249bade) per-state colour map lookups that entered render on the sheet paths: the alert sheet''s reminder cards ride per-state colour tables resolved per render.
- H4 (322, e7993f59) the sheets: the header labels'' new ink tweens (Day''s location, Countdown''s prayer name) ride the same derived machinery, and the colour modal''s pre-composited backdrop changed what every sheet entrance composites. The alpha-0 sweep is build-time validation and cannot regress runtime, so reading exonerates it.
- H5 anything else inside the window the anchors name. The list above is where the evidence points first, not what it concludes.

Fix candidates, chosen only after the cause is named, each preserving D5 and the repo''s visual settlement (fixes change behaviour, not pixels; animated components first-frame in their settled state; only value changes animate):
- one veil progress per row shared by all its ink styles, replacing two derived values per element
- hoisted or pre-parsed colour inputs to interpolateColor
- memoised per-state colour resolution off the render path
- the display:none drop batched after every fade has settled

Alternatives rejected:
- Reverting the veil to opacity fades: violates the pinned solid-ink invariant and reddens yarn validate (D5).
- Concluding from code reading: the dictation itself says the investigation owns the truth; the 3T''s history (the phantom Choreographer loop, the mock confounds) has produced false attributions before, and the baselines predate the whole window.
- Measuring on the emulator: banned by the harness; every perf number names a physical device.
- Measuring on debug or prod builds: debug cadence is meaningless and prod folds the marks out (D6).

## Steps

Points: 1 docs, 2 code, 3 device. Every device step runs alone in a fresh session, one device at a time. Every build goes through the single slot (D6). e2e/README.md is re-read before every measurement step; e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md before any 3T screen work.

1. Step 1: the tip''s numbers on the 3T (3 points, device). Build Release gate-ON at origin/uat tip (1c22014c) per e2e/README.md''s build block: clear the Metro cache and the generated bundle, EXPO_PUBLIC_PERF_MONITOR=1, install with adb install -r after the badging assert of D8, then the User 0 assert and the versionName check before measuring. Discard the first post-install launch. Verify PERF_MEASURE lines flow (adb logcat -s ReactNativeJS) before driving anything. Run baseline-compare.sh on overlay-x10.yaml and sheets-x10.yaml. Frame-audit overlay-open (tap 540 974); frame-audit overlay-close through the pre-tap open mode added to e2e/scripts/frame-audit.sh (open at 540 974, wait out the entrance, then record the closing tap at 540 1100, per overlay-x10''s drive); frame-audit sheet-alert-open (979 974) and sheet-settings-open (540 1730). The video path with the vision subagent reading each contact sheet is the verdict; FRAME_AUDIT=sf only as the labelled fallback of D2. Produces: which marks regressed against e2e/baselines/android-3t.json and which floors fail, with the evidence dirs recorded.
2. Step 2: the XS before-picture (3 points, device). The same tip as a Release configuration build with EXPO_PUBLIC_PERF_MONITOR=1 per e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md. Install, then discard the first post-install launch (the What''s New gotcha is platform-neutral). First act of measurement: the atlas carries no Athan-app tap points on the XS, so measure the four tap points (a prayer row that opens the overlay, the closing row, the settings button, the alert bell) by screenshot with the vision subagent reading them, and write them into e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md; snapshots wedge on the countdown home screen, so screenshot-plus-vision is the read, never a live snapshot. Then drive ten iterations of each of the four interactions through agent-device by the recorded points; capture PERF_MEASURE through pymobiledevice3 syslog live (tag Athan{React}); run the capture twice to establish each mark''s spread. Produces: the four before-medians and their band, the line "unchanged" is judged against, plus the atlas rows. The owner''s eyeball rides the same build.
3. Step 3: the anchor bisect on the 3T (3 points, device). Measure f97cd7d4 (294 merged) first, the owner''s suspicion. Regressed: measure 5b496afe next; still regressed there widens the loop backwards (D3), clean there puts the window at 5b496afe..f97cd7d4. Clean at f97cd7d4: measure 887d7949 (322 merged); the window becomes f97cd7d4..887d7949. Per anchor: worktree at the commit, yarn install, the same build ritual and asserts as Step 1, adb install -r (add -d if the candidate ever predates the installed build''s versionCode; the code is flat 1000000 across this window), discard the first launch, baseline-compare both flows, frame-audit the interactions Step 1 named failing. Produces: the ticket window that owns the regression.
4. Step 4: the commit bisect on the 3T (3 points, device). Halve the owning window''s commits; per candidate, build and install the same way, discard the first launch, then the failing audits and marks only. Produces: the regressing commit or commits named by measurement, with each candidate''s numbers.
5. Step 5: the root cause named and the fix implemented (2 points, code). Name the cause with frame evidence: what work entered the tap path or the animation frame, on which thread (ReactNativeJS versus native in the logcat, the frame gaps in the audits), from which change (the commit the bisect named, read against the hypothesis list). Implement the fix under D5 and the visual settlement, red-first coverage on every line touched, a mutation pass on guarded logic, yarn validate green. Produces: the fix commits on the lane branch.
6. Step 6: post-fix proof on the 3T and the baselines refreshed (3 points, device). Release gate-ON build of the fix; the four frame audits pass the 30fps floor of D2''s video-path observable, zero gaps over 33ms with 16-17ms cadence the target, vision-read contact sheets; the marks sit inside the baseline band. Re-base e2e/baselines/android-3t.json''s medians and floors with a dated note; overlay_close_steady''s UNPROVEN verdict gets its corrected video-path run here. Produces: the passing audits and the refreshed baselines.
7. Step 7: the XS after-picture (3 points, device). The same fix build and the same drive as Step 2, both capture runs, first launch discarded, the atlas''s recorded points. Produces: the four after-medians inside Step 2''s band, read side by side, and the owner''s eyeball on the same build.
8. Step 8: close-out on the final branch (2 points, code). yarn validate green on the final branch; e2e/README.md''s Gotchas gains any trap the investigation learned, only when one was learned; the version bumped per D7; the ticket''s records complete. Produces: the finished branch ready for audit.

22 points total: two code steps, six device steps.

## Risks

- The regression does not reproduce on the harness build: the phone''s state differs (a Dual Messenger parallel copy, a stale Android Studio screen-sharing agent burning CPU, thermal state). Step 1 measuring clean shows it. Then check top for app_process screensharing agents and the dumpsys package user list before any code conclusion, and report rather than bisect.
- Video capture wedges on the 3T (known since s6): a reboot restores it; FRAME_AUDIT=sf still works, but one SF run is one sample, never a verdict on its own; the video path plus a vision read stands behind any SF result recorded as a verdict.
- The bisect window widens past 294 and 322: each anchor costs one build-and-measure cycle; the loop is unchanged, only longer.
- Marks mislead: D2 keeps every verdict off the overlay_open mark; the floors are compositor truth.
- The fix trades cost for a snap: the first-frame-settled rule and the 150/200ms feel are pinned by suites, and the vision read catches a snap in Step 6''s contact sheets.
- The XS band is too loose to prove anything: two before-runs establish the spread; when the spread swamps the delta, run a third capture rather than widen the claim.
- Two builds at once: the single-slot rule (D6). A queued executor waits for the slot; a slot conflict is a stop-and-report, never a race.

## Proof

- Acceptance 1 (baseline-compare names the regressed marks, the commits identified by measurement or bisect): Step 1''s two compare.json tables against e2e/baselines/android-3t.json, and Step 4''s per-candidate tables naming the commit where the numbers flip.
- Acceptance 2 (the root cause named with frame evidence): Step 5''s record citing the failing audit''s gap list (under e2e/evidence/), the thread the work landed on (logcat tags), and the named commit''s diff.
- Acceptance 3 (overlay open and close pass the 30fps floor on a Release gate-ON build): Step 6''s video-path frame audits printing "gaps>33ms: NONE", each contact sheet vision-read monotonic with no snap.
- Acceptance 4 (the alert and settings sheets pass the same floor): Step 6''s sheet audits, the same printed verdicts and vision reads.
- Acceptance 5 (the iPhone XS measurably unchanged): Step 7''s four after-medians against Step 2''s recorded band, in the ticket''s record.
- Acceptance 6 (yarn validate green): yarn validate exits 0 on the final branch, Step 8.

## Grill findings answered

- 2026-10-24, finding 1 (no PASS observable on the video path): fixed. D2 and Proof now define the pass as the printed "gaps>33ms: NONE" plus the vision-read contact sheet; the SF PASS line stays a labelled fallback.
- 2026-10-24, finding 2 (the close audit had no executable drive): fixed. frame-audit.sh gains a pre-tap open mode, authorized in Changed, and Step 1 names its use.
- 2026-10-24, finding 3 (no XS tap points, snapshots wedge): fixed. Step 2''s first act measures the four points by screenshot-plus-vision and writes them into the XS atlas; the drive replays them.
- 2026-10-24, finding 4 (first-launch discard missing on the XS): fixed. Steps 2 and 7 both discard it.
- 2026-10-24, finding 5 (badging rule contradiction): fixed. D8 scopes the fleettest stop to owner-daily installs and names the harness assert.
- 2026-10-24, finding 6 (Lane unset): already false on the board, the field write landed 2026-10-24 before the grill; the MCP read path returns fieldValues empty for every ticket including ones the snapshot proves carry values, so the lead verifies it at the phase boundary.
