```sh
curl -s "https://www.londonprayertimes.com/api/times?format=json&key=$(tr -d '' \n\r'' < ~/.config/athan/.api_key)&year=2026&24hours=true"
```
Transcribe into a ticket comment: the six times for 24, 25 and 26 Oct; the Extras Midnight and Last Third instants for the 24-25 night; Fajr 25 Oct in GMT (the Step 5 time-box); the expected countdown target at R1 for both schedules. `yarn validate` green. No production code changes.

**Step 2** (device, 3). Version bump per the decision above. Build the iOS prod Release per the atlas "Device build" and "Device build-only" rows: prebuild, `EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=prod`, `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_KEY` from the key file into the process env only, `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` inline, xcodebuild for a device artifact, `xcrun devicectl device install app` on `IPHONE_UDID`. The iOS build precedes any 3T build tonight (`build-prod.zsh` refuses to start beside an xcodebuild, and the slot rule is never two at once). Launch once, compare the screen against Step 1''s transcription to prove real times served and stored, leave it foregrounded to finish sync and arming. Read the bell state; enable both schedules'' at-time athans when off, prior state recorded. Pre-crossing readings 23:45-23:59 BST: both schedules'' full lists and day labels, both countdown targets, the home screen, the overlay. Midnight rollover: reads at 23:58 and 00:03 BST transcribing the day label move Sat 24 to Sun 25 on both schedules, the Standard countdown target moving to Fajr, the lists swapping days. All reads are screenshots (snapshots wedge on the countdown); the atlas''s traps section governs.

**Step 3** (device, 3). Session opens 01:45, app foregrounded on the Standard page. At R1, R2 (bracketed), R3, R4 transcribe from screenshots: wall clock and UTC; countdown target name and remaining on both schedules; day label on both schedules; both schedules'' row lists; the overlay at R1 and R4; the home screen at R3 when a widget sits on it; every notification that fires in the window with its lock-screen timestamp (the Last Third row of the 24 Oct night may fire near R2 when armed - transcribe it; expected otherwise none before Fajr). The countdown must not stall or jump: R1 to R2 and R2 to R3 each consume 300 real seconds. The day label and list content at R3/R4 must equal the first pass''s. Comment the transcription on the ticket before the session ends. 3T extension, only on the lead''s handover before 23:45, sequenced after the iOS build: `$HOME/athan-gitree/bin/build-prod.zsh <ref> <out.apk>`, install on `3T_SERIAL`, assert User 0 alone per the repo command, read `e2e/device-atlas-oneplus3t.md` first, then the same four instants from the 3T screen plus `yarn check:device 3T_SERIAL "$APP_ID" <expected-times.json>` alarm dumps at R1 and R4 with trigger times checked against Step 1''s transcription.

**Step 4** (device, 3). Foreground the app: day label Sun 25 Oct on both schedules, lists equal to Step 1''s transcription, countdown targeting the day''s next prayer. Airplane mode on, relaunch: the stored rows alone serve the same day offline (the offline invariant is the stored-rows proof on iOS), lists identical to the online read; airplane off after. Transcribe the day''s remaining prayers displaying. Restore the bell state changed in Step 2. Transcribe the 3T''s post-crossing alarm dump when the extension ran.

**Step 5** (device, 3). From Fajr-10 to Fajr+10 GMT (Step 1''s value). Lock the phone with the side button (the XS never auto-locks while tethered; manual lock works), app in the background. Transcribe the Fajr athan notification and its lock-screen timestamp, compared against the API''s Fajr. Unlock, foreground, transcribe the countdown target advancing past Fajr. This step is the fire-on-time proof; when nothing fires, transcribe the phone''s notification settings state for the app and record the criterion unproven on iOS, with the 3T alarm dump as the fallback evidence when the extension ran.

**Step 6** (docs, 1). One comment per acceptance criterion naming its evidence: suite output lines, the Step 1 transcription, the rollover, R1-R4, the post reads, the Fajr fire. Verdict per criterion; every defect named with its follow-up ticket reference. `yarn validate` re-run when anything changed after Step 1.

## Risks

- The iOS build overruns 01:30: the crossing is then watched on whatever prod build the XS already carries, its build identity recorded from Settings; when the installed build is mock or unknown, the live criteria are recorded partial and the static proof carries the ticket. No clock is ever set by hand.
- A gap test exposes a real defect: recorded, follow-up ticket, no fix inside the window.
- Lane 2 contention on the Mac or the 3T: the optional path does not run; the iPhone path never waits on it.
- The XS arrives with a stale dev-cache: a previous mock build''s rows live in `athan-storage-dev` and are never read by a prod build; the Step 2 screen comparison proves the prod store served real values.
- The Last Third notification is not armed (bell off before Step 2, or the budget spent elsewhere): the fire evidence rests on Step 5''s Fajr.
- A reading is missed at an instant: the screenshot timestamps and the ticket comment carry what was caught; the window is not extended past 02:20.

## Proof

- Static suites on the tip: `yarn test:tz` green; `yarn jest shared/__tests__/time.test.ts -t "fall" --silent` and the notifications budget filter each report "N passed" with N > 0; the three gap tests land red first, then green, committed with the run transcripts in the ticket.
- Before the crossing: the Step 1 curl transcription equals the XS screen read in Step 2 (both schedules, both countdowns, day labels); the build report lines and the install output recorded.
- Through the crossing: the Step 3 comment carries four timestamped reading sets; countdown deltas of 300 real seconds R1-R2 and R2-R3; identical day label and list content across the two 01:xx passes; every firing notification transcribed.
- After the crossing: the Step 4 comment carries the online read, the airplane-mode relaunch read, and the remaining prayers; the 3T alarm dump shows every remaining prayer armed at its true local time when the extension ran.
- Fire on time: the Step 5 comment carries the Fajr notification transcript against the API''s Fajr value.
- Gates: `yarn validate` green in Step 1 and re-run in Step 6; all findings recorded on this ticket as they happen.
