INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (112, 40, 1, NULL, 'T-346 - the prayer-ago badge keeps its space around the time in every language, and Hindi stays on one line on Android', '# T-346 - The prayer-ago badge keeps its space around the time in every language, and Hindi stays on one line on Android

## Goal

Today two visual defects sit in the time-ago badge below the prayer list. Thai on both platforms renders the sentence''s trailing word touching the interpolated time''s last letter with no space: `shared/i18n/th.ts`''s `time.ago` is `''{name} {duration}ที่แล้ว''`, so the byte after `{duration}` is a Thai consonant, while the other five locales space the token or end the string at it. Hindi on Android only wraps the badge into two lines with the second cropped to a sliver, because the badge Text in `components/prayer/Ago.tsx` carries no one-line constraint and Android''s text engine breaks the sentence at a space. When this is done, every shipped locale''s `time.ago` template holds a space (or the string''s edge) on both sides of the `{duration}` token - gated for all six locales and any future one - and the badge never wraps: one line on every platform, the pill growing into the room it has.

## Decisions taken

- 2026-10-25 - The spacing rule is enforced as a catalog gate over every locale''s `time.ago` template, not in `compose`. Why: the interpolated time is the `{duration}` token of one key; injecting spaces at composition would change every interpolated string in the app (channel names, steppers, reminders) across six locales, while the gate holds the owner''s general rule - any text adjacent to the time is separated by a space - for every catalog the key set admits, present and future.
- 2026-10-25 - The gate accepts the string''s edge as a valid neighbor. Why: Arabic ends the sentence at the time (`''{name} قبل {duration}''`) and the owner''s reference read lists Arabic as spacing correctly; the defect is text touching the time, and a string edge touches nothing. Thai''s defect is a consonant byte, which the gate refuses.
- 2026-10-25 - The one-line mechanism is `numberOfLines={1}` on the badge''s Animated.Text. Why: it is the platform''s own never-wrap contract; the pill already grows with its content (`alignSelf: ''center''` under the page''s full width), so the constraint buys horizontal growth in the room the owner names. `adjustsFontSizeToFit` is iOS-only and would change glyph sizes; a maxHeight clip would hide bytes; both rejected. T-345''s rejection of a numberOfLines guard was for a title the owner reserved; here the owner''s own acceptance line orders the one-line constraint.
- 2026-10-25 - The badge''s inner component is exported for the suite. Why: `PrayerAgoBadge` already exists as the unit boundary that takes the composed string; the suite renders it under all six locales without the store, the clock or the locale switcher. Precedent: `calculatePrayerAgo` is exported "so tests can call the real thing" (hooks/usePrayerAgo.ts:19).
- 2026-10-25 - The device read is Step 3 and waits for the build slot. Why: the owner''s reference reads are the S23 (Thai, Hindi) and the XS (Thai); a mock build (both platforms, `build-mock.zsh`) driven on those phones is the final proof of the rendered badge; Lane 1 (T-327) holds the device slot and the step waits rather than contending. The unit layers prove the string and the constraint; the phone proves the pixels.
- 2026-10-25 - The bump path is package.json + app.json + `shared/whatsNew.ts`''s `WHATS_NEW.version`, not android/app/build.gradle. Why: `/android` is gitignored prebuild output (recorded in T-345''s plan, verified with `git check-ignore`), so no commit can carry it; app.json plus prebuild is the real path. A bump that adds no whats-new item silent-ships by construction.

## Files

- `shared/i18n/th.ts` - the one-byte fix: `''time.ago''` gains a space after `{duration}`.
- `shared/__tests__/catalogGates.test.ts` - the new spacing gate over every locale''s `time.ago` template.
- `components/prayer/Ago.tsx` - `numberOfLines={1}` on the badge''s Animated.Text; `PrayerAgoBadge` exported for the suite.
- `components/prayer/__tests__/Ago.test.tsx` - new suite: six locales'' composed ago strings render under the one-line constraint.
- `package.json`, `app.json`, `shared/whatsNew.ts` - the patch version bump each commit carries.
- `scripts/version-collisions-allowlist.json` - an entry if another lane''s stamp twins mine (record the interleaving, renumber above whatever uat carries).
- Read, proven untouched: `hooks/usePrayerAgo.ts` (composes the string), `shared/i18n/index.ts` (`compose`, `tIn`), `shared/time.ts` (`formatTimeAgo` wraps the duration in U+2066/U+2069 isolates), `__tests__/app/Screen.test.tsx` (the badge''s existing coverage), `shared/__tests__/i18nBridge.test.ts` (token parity - tokens unchanged).

## Design

The invariant, in two halves.

Spacing: the only place the time value enters user-facing copy is the `{duration}` token of the `time.ago` catalog key (the badge''s `time.now` half interpolates the prayer name only; `usePrayerAgo.ts:38`). The rendered duration arrives from `formatTimeAgo` wrapped in Unicode isolates (\u2066...\u2069, zero-width), so whatever byte neighbors `{duration}` in the template neighbors the time''s first and last visible glyph on screen. The gate therefore reads the template: for every catalog (en, ar, ms, so, hi, th), the byte before `{duration}` is a space or the string''s start, and the byte after is a space or the string''s end. Today th fails on the trailing side and no other locale fails; the fix is the single space in th''s template. The gate joins the R2 gates in `catalogGates.test.ts`, which every locale must already pass to land, so a seventh locale that touches the time inherits the rule - general, never language-specific.

One line: the badge is an `Animated.Text` styled as a pill (`alignSelf: ''center''`, `paddingHorizontal`, `borderRadius: pill`, `overflow: ''hidden''`) under the page''s full width. It carries no line constraint, so Android''s text engine is free to break the Hindi sentence at a space and crop the second line against the pill''s radius; iOS does not break it. `numberOfLines={1}` removes the engine''s freedom: the Text lays out its content on one line and takes that width, the pill grows to wrap it, and on iOS - where every locale already renders one line - the constraint changes no pixel. The suite renders `PrayerAgoBadge` once per locale with that locale''s own composed ago string (via `tIn`) and asserts the rendered Text carries `numberOfLines={1}` and shows exactly the composed string, so the constraint is proven against every locale''s real bytes, Thai''s isolates included.

Alternatives rejected: injecting spaces in `compose` (blast radius across every interpolated key, above); a per-locale width table (the ticket bans language-specific rules); `adjustsFontSizeToFit` (iOS-only, changes glyph size); `maxHeight` clipping (hides bytes rather than refusing the wrap).

## Steps

1. **Step 1: the time-ago spacing gate and the Thai byte (2 points)** - the gate in `catalogGates.test.ts` over all six locales'' `time.ago` (red on th''s trailing edge first), then the one-byte fix in `th.ts`, then the mutation pass: revert the Thai byte and watch the gate fail; strip a leading space from a compliant locale in memory and watch it fail on the leading edge; put the token at both string edges and watch it pass. Version bump 2.4.45, renumbered above whatever uat carries at commit time.
2. **Step 2: the one-line badge constraint and its suite (2 points)** - export `PrayerAgoBadge`, add `numberOfLines={1}`, and write `Ago.test.tsx`: for each of the six locales, compose the ago string with `tIn` and assert the badge renders exactly that string under `numberOfLines={1}` (red first: the prop is absent today); mutation: remove the prop and watch the suite fail. `Screen.test.tsx` and `usePrayerAgo.test.ts` stay green untouched. `yarn validate` green. Version bump, same renumbering rule.
3. **Step 3: the device reads on the S23 and the XS (3 points)** - wait for the build slot (Lane 1/T-327 holds it; confirm no build runs: `pgrep -fl ''assembleRelease|xcodebuild''`), build mock both platforms via `$HOME/athan-gitree/bin/build-mock.zsh`, read the device atlases (`e2e/device-atlas-sm-s911b.md`, `e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md`), switch the app''s language to Hindi and Thai, and transcribe: Hindi''s badge on one line on the S23 with no cropped second line, Thai''s badge with a space before and after the time on both the S23 and the XS. Readings land on the ticket; no screenshot is committed; no tree change, no bump.

## Risks

