INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (127, 47, 1, NULL, 'T-400', '# T-400 - the lock screen widgets'' type scale

## Goal

Today every live reading on the lock screen accessory faces renders at a nominal 14pt, and layouts 1 and 2 carry a `minimumScaleFactor(0.6)` floor that shrinks a long name or countdown to 8.4pt on glass. Users report the type reads too small. When this is done: the live faces render at a nominal 16-17pt per format, no live reading ever renders below today''s nominal 14pt, the home screen widgets and Android are untouched, the widget runtime load suite and `yarn validate` pass, and a glass read on the iPhone XS is transcribed on the ticket.

## Decisions taken

- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) Read split: sim measures, XS verifies.** Athan-76 (iPhone 16, iOS 18.5, the closest runtime to the XS''s 18.7) carries the measurement pass, because maestro drives simulators and the pixel-to-point conversion is exact there. The XS carries the on-glass verification of the landed change, because the atlas rules its true lock screen unreachable (wake traps, T-337) and the owner''s later eyeball is final anyway. The ticket''s own text allows either device.
- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) Read surface on the XS: Settings > Wallpaper > Customize.** The atlas records that no wake route reaches the true lock screen on this passcode-less phone; the customize sheet renders the real widgets from the real timeline. The transcription states it was read there. On the sim, the true lock screen is reached by placing the widgets then locking; if no headless lock route works (simctl carries none documented), the same customize sheet on the sim is the read, with the screenshot''s pixel-to-point calibration stated.
- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) The floor never reads smaller than today''s nominal.** Every raised nominal carries `minimumScaleFactor` set so nominal x floor >= 14: layouts 1 and 2 use 0.82 (17 x 0.82 = 13.94), layout 3''s name-and-time row gains a new 0.88 floor (16 x 0.88 = 14.08). The users'' complaint is about the small end, so the small end is what must rise: the worst case after this change reads no smaller than the common case before it.
- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) Per-format ceilings: 17 / 17 / 16, stale and neutral +1, inline stands.** Layouts 1 and 2 are single-row halves with all of the slot''s height free, so they take 17. Layout 3 stacks the longest row in the widget ("Last Third 23:52") and caps at 16, the ceiling the owner''s direction anticipates. The stale and neutral cards rise one point (17/14 to 18/15, 11/17 to 12/18) behind the measured-fit condition below. The inline face stays 14: it renders in a fixed-height system band that Apple''s own inline accessories fill at system-chosen sizes near 14, and a bigger nominal there clips rather than shrinks; step 1''s measurement overturns this ruling only if the measured inline band carries 15pt with no clipping.
- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) The home screen widgets, the Android widget and every string are untouched.** The owner''s direction is styling only, lock screen only. No new strings, no layout restructure, no schedule change; only `font` sizes, the two floors, and the new layout-3 floor.

## Files

- `widgets/LockPrayerWidget.tsx` - the type scale: live faces of all three layouts, the stale and neutral cards per the conditionals, floors.
- `shared/__tests__/widgetLockRenderer.test.ts` - the new size and floor pins, written red first.
- `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` - the version bump, patch, all three together.

## Design

The three lock layout functions each serialize alone (''widget'' directive), so each function''s sizes are edited in place; no shared constant is introduced across layouts, matching the file''s standing rule.

Exact changes:

1. `AthanLockWidgetCountdownPair` live rectangular (layout 1): name `font({ size: 17, weight: ''bold'' })`, ticking countdown `font({ size: 17, weight: ''medium'' })`, both `minimumScaleFactor(0.6)` to `minimumScaleFactor(0.82)`. Weights, colours, frames, paddings and the midline halves stay exactly as they are.
2. `AthanLockWidgetCentred` live rectangular (layout 2): name 17 bold, absolute time 17 medium monospaced, floor 0.6 to 0.82, same invariants.
3. `AthanLockWidgetStacked` live rectangular (layout 3): name, absolute time and countdown 14 to 16; the name and time Texts gain `minimumScaleFactor(0.88)` (they carry none today, so a too-big nominal would truncate a prayer name - data loss - where a floor shrinks it). The countdown keeps `lineLimit(1)` with no floor.
4. Stale card, all three layouts: title 17 to 18, body 14 to 15, icon 17 to 18. Condition: applied only when step 1''s measured slot height minus the measured current stale stack leaves at least 3pt; otherwise only the title rises to 18 and the body and icon stand.
5. Neutral card, all three layouts: rectTitle 11 to 12, rectSubtitle 17 to 18. Unconditional: the two-row stack fits the slot at every measured size.
6. Every inline face stays 14 per the ruling above.
7. Tests: `widgetLockRenderer.test.ts` gains a table pinning, per live layout and family, every Text''s nominal font size and minimumScaleFactor value, plus the stale and neutral pins per the applied branch. The pins are written first and shown red against the current code, then the code change turns them green. Each pin flipped (17 to 16, 0.82 to 0.6, 16 to 15) fails its assertion - that is the mutation pass, recorded in the run''s log line.

The invariant: the rendered hierarchy (weight and opacity tiers, muted second readings, centring, midline seams) is byte-identical except the size numbers and the two floors.

## Steps

1. **Step 1: Measured baseline of the lock widgets'' current type on Athan-76** (3 points, device). Build the current uat to Athan-76 (`npx expo run:ios`, simulator route, build lock taken), place one Standard and one Extras lock widget on the lock screen via maestro, screenshot the live faces, and record on the ticket: the rectangular slot''s width and height in pt, the rendered cap heights of the name, second reading and countdown per layout in pt, the stale stack''s height, the inline band''s height, and the current effective range (nominal 14, floor 8.4 on layouts 1-2). This is acceptance criterion 1.
2. **Step 2: The lock type scale raised with suite pins, load suite and validate green, version bump, lane commit** (2 points, code). Write the pins red, apply the change per Design (branch 4 decided by step 1''s measurement), `yarn jest shared/__tests__/widgetLockRenderer.test.ts` green with the pins, `yarn jest shared/__tests__/widgetRuntimeLoads.test.ts` green, `yarn validate` green, the mutation flips fail as specified. Fetch origin, re-read `package.json` (Lane 2 bumps in parallel), take the next free patch across the three version files, commit on the lane branch.
3. **Step 3: Both-platform mock build, XS glass read transcribed, merged to uat** (3 points, device). Under the build lock: `zsh $HOME/athan-gitree/bin/build-mock.zsh <lane-sha> mocks/simple.ts <out.apk>` for the Android half, and the standing `$HOME/athan-gitree/worktrees/ios-build` moved to the lane SHA for the iOS half, both compilers in parallel inside the lock. Verify the built iOS bundle id before install, install to the XS via `xcrun devicectl`, launch, confirm the timeline push in `pymobiledevice3 syslog live` (tag `Athan`), read the widgets in Settings > Wallpaper > Customize via the agent-device runner, transcribe the read on the ticket, then merge the lane branch to local uat (no push) and move the ticket to Audit.

## Risks

- A raised nominal truncates instead of shrinking where no floor exists. Layout 3''s name-and-time row is the only such spot and it gains the 0.88 floor; the pins hold it.
- The stale card''s one-point rise overflows the slot on a short slot. The 3pt-slack condition in Design branch 4 measures before it applies.
- Long-locale strings ("Fur si aad u soo dejinto waqtiyada") truncate on the stale card today and still will; the change neither fixes nor worsens that materially, and the complaint under work is the live readings.
- StandBy renders these same layouts at its own larger scale; they grow there too, which the direction''s "much bigger" wants.
- Lane 2 takes the same patch number. The re-read-and-take-next-free rule in Step 2 covers it; any interleaving is recorded in the ticket''s audit comment.
- The XS read route breaks if the agent-device runner fails to prepare (the MCP server is already broken this session; the CLI answered its help text). Fallback: the Athan-76 sim read stands as the glass read, and the ticket records why, the ticket''s text allowing a simulator read.

## Proof

- `yarn jest shared/__tests__/widgetLockRenderer.test.ts -t "sizes"` - the new pins reported skipped-or-failing before the change (red) and passing after, with the `N passed` line read per the e2e gotcha.
- `yarn jest shared/__tests__/widgetRuntimeLoads.test.ts` - evaluates on android and on ios, both green.
- `yarn validate` - green.
- Step 1''s comment on T-400 - the measured pt table.
- Step 3''s comment on T-400 - the transcribed XS read naming the customize sheet as the surface.
- `git log uat -1` - the merge commit carrying the lane branch.
