INSERT INTO public.project_document_revision (id, document_id, version, parent_id, title, content, content_json, icon, metadata, full_width, is_private, is_locked, archived_at, "position", owner_user_id, created_by_user_id, created_at) VALUES (133, 47, 3, NULL, 'T-400', '# T-400 - the lock screen widgets'' type scale

## Goal

Today every live reading on the lock screen accessory faces renders at a nominal 14pt, and layouts 1 and 2 carry a `minimumScaleFactor(0.6)` floor that shrinks a long name or countdown to 8.4pt on glass. Users report the type reads too small. When this is done: the live faces render at a nominal 16-17pt per format, no live reading ever renders below today''s nominal 14pt (nominal x floor >= 14), the home screen widgets and Android are untouched, the widget runtime load suite and `yarn validate` pass, and a glass read of the landed change is transcribed on the ticket.

## Decisions taken

- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) Read split: sim measures, XS verifies.** Athan-76 (iPhone 16, iOS 18.5, the closest runtime to the XS''s 18.7) carries the measurement pass, because maestro drives simulators and the pixel-to-point conversion is exact there. The XS carries the on-glass verification of the landed change, because the atlas rules its true lock screen unreachable (wake traps, T-337) and the owner''s later eyeball is final anyway.
- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) Read surface: Settings > Wallpaper > Customize on both devices.** The atlas records that no wake route reaches the XS''s true lock screen on this passcode-less phone; the customize sheet renders the real widgets from the real timeline, with the widget boxes outlined, so the slot box is measurable there. On the sim the same sheet is the read (simctl documents no headless lock, and a simulator follows the host clock, so the true lock screen is not reachable there either). Every transcription names the customize sheet as its surface, and the screenshot''s pixel-to-point scale is stated with each number.
- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) The floor never reads smaller than today''s nominal.** Every raised nominal carries `minimumScaleFactor` set so nominal x floor >= 14: layouts 1 and 2 use 0.83 (17 x 0.83 = 14.11), layout 3''s live texts use 0.88 (16 x 0.88 = 14.08). The users'' complaint is about the small end, so the small end is what must rise: the worst case after this change reads no smaller than the common case before it.
- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) Per-format ceilings: 17 / 17 / 16, stale and neutral +1, inline stands.** Layouts 1 and 2 are single-row halves with all of the slot''s height free, so they take 17. Layout 3 stacks the longest row in the widget ("Last Third 23:52") and caps at 16, the ceiling the owner''s direction anticipates. The stale and neutral cards rise one point (17/14 to 18/15, 11/17 to 12/18), decided arithmetically below. The inline face stays 14 with no overturn clause: it renders in a fixed-height system band at system-chosen sizes near 14, a bigger nominal there clips rather than shrinks, and no planned read produces an inline measurement anyway.
- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) The stale-card rise is decided by arithmetic, not by an on-glass measurement.** A simulator follows the host clock and the mock''s stale window opens only at 23:53, so no planned step can render the stale card. The slot height is measured from the customize sheet''s outlined widget box; the stale stack''s height is computed as the sum of SF Pro line heights (1.2 x size per text, 1.0 x size for the icon) plus the 1pt spacings. The +1 rise applies when measured slot height minus computed current stack >= 3pt; otherwise only the title rises to 18. Both branches are exact and the applied branch is recorded in the step''s comment.
- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) The home screen widgets, the Android widget and every string are untouched.** The owner''s direction is styling only, lock screen only. No new strings, no layout restructure, no schedule change; only `font` sizes and the floors.
- **agent-ruled (2026-10-28) The mock iOS build installs beside, not over: EXPO_IOS_SUFFIX=fleettest.** iOS refuses a dev-signed install over the store-signed app (app.config.ts), so the build takes the suffix pattern that mirrors the Android fleettest convention. Its widgets are separate widget kinds, so the read replaces the XS lock screen''s widgets with the fleettest app''s and restores the previous configuration afterwards. Expected bundle id: com.$BUNDLE.athan.fleettest.

## Files

- `widgets/LockPrayerWidget.tsx` - the type scale: live faces of all three layouts, the stale and neutral cards per the arithmetic branch, floors.
- `shared/__tests__/widgetLockRenderer.test.ts` - the new size and floor pins, written red first, their test names carrying "sizes" so the `-t` filter proves they ran.
- `e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md` - the Settings > Wallpaper > Customize route written back after the read, per the atlas''s own footer.
- `plugins/duoTallCanvas.js` and `plugins/__tests__/duoTallCanvas.test.ts` - the fleettest path sanitization Step 3 forced (a suffixed build''s mods died reading an unsanitized directory name), its own red-first wiring row; amended into Files at audit, 2026-10-28.
- `package.json`, `app.json`, `android/app/build.gradle` - the version bump, patch, all three together.

## Design

The three lock layout functions each serialize alone (''widget'' directive), so each function''s sizes are edited in place; no shared constant is introduced across layouts, matching the file''s standing rule.

Exact changes:

1. `AthanLockWidgetCountdownPair` live rectangular (layout 1): name `font({ size: 17, weight: ''bold'' })`, ticking countdown `font({ size: 17, weight: ''medium'' })`, both `minimumScaleFactor(0.6)` to `minimumScaleFactor(0.83)`. Weights, colours, frames, paddings and the midline halves stay exactly as they are.
2. `AthanLockWidgetCentred` live rectangular (layout 2): name 17 bold, absolute time 17 medium monospaced, floor 0.6 to 0.83, same invariants.
3. `AthanLockWidgetStacked` live rectangular (layout 3): name, absolute time and countdown 14 to 16; all three Texts gain `minimumScaleFactor(0.88)` (they carry none today, so a too-big nominal would truncate a prayer name - data loss - where a floor shrinks it; the countdown gets the same floor for uniformity even though its fixed-format seven-glyph worst case cannot overflow the slot).
4. Stale card, all three layouts: title 17 to 18, body 14 to 15, icon 17 to 18, behind the arithmetic branch in Decisions; the applied branch is recorded in Step 1''s comment.
5. Neutral card, all three layouts: rectTitle 11 to 12, rectSubtitle 17 to 18. Unconditional: the two-row stack fits the slot at every measured size.
6. Every inline face stays 14, no exception.
7. Tests: `widgetLockRenderer.test.ts` gains a pin table whose test names all carry "sizes", pinning per live layout and family every Text''s nominal font size and minimumScaleFactor value, plus the stale and neutral pins per the applied branch. The pins are written first and shown red against the current code, then the code change turns them green. Each pin flipped (17 to 16, 0.83 to 0.6, 16 to 15) fails its assertion - that is the mutation pass, recorded in the run''s log line.

The invariant: the rendered hierarchy (weight and opacity tiers, muted second readings, centring, midline seams) is byte-identical except the size numbers and the floors.

## Steps

The run''s inter-lane build lock (the lead''s protocol for this run, backstopped by AGENTS.md''s toolchain-collision rule): `mkdir $HOME/athan-gitree/.build-lock` before any build command, recheck every 60s while held, `rmdir` the moment the command returns.

1. **Step 1: Measured baseline of the lock widgets'' current type on Athan-76** (3 points, device). Build uat''s HEAD from the lane worktree to Athan-76 with `EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=local EXPO_PUBLIC_IOS_WIDGETS=1 npx expo run:ios` (a `.env` written into the lane worktree carrying the same two flags covers prebuild-time reads; without the widgets flag the extension is stripped and the placed widgets render the neutral card forever). Place one lock widget at a time via the customize sheet (maestro drives): Standard `PrayerLockWidget`, then `PrayerLockWidget2`, then `PrayerLockWidget3`, then Extras `ExtrasLockWidget3` (the longest names: Last Third, Midnight), screenshotting each live face plus the outlined slot box. Record on the ticket: the rectangular slot''s width and height in pt (from the outlined box), the rendered cap heights of the name, second reading and countdown per layout in pt, the computed stale stack height and the applied stale branch, and the current effective range (nominal 14, floor 8.4 on layouts 1-2). This is acceptance criterion 1.
2. **Step 2: The lock type scale raised with suite pins, load suite and validate green, version bump, lane commit** (2 points, code). Write the pins red, apply the change per Design, `yarn jest shared/__tests__/widgetLockRenderer.test.ts -t "sizes"` green with the new pins counted in the `N passed` line, `yarn jest shared/__tests__/widgetRuntimeLoads.test.ts` green, `yarn validate` green, the mutation flips fail as specified. Fetch origin, re-read `package.json` (Lane 2 bumps in parallel), take the next free patch across the three version files, commit on the lane branch.
3. **Step 3: Both-platform mock build, XS glass read transcribed, atlas route written back, merged to uat** (3 points, device). Under the build lock, both compilers in parallel: Android via `zsh $HOME/athan-gitree/bin/build-mock.zsh <lane-sha> mocks/simple.ts <out.apk>` (built to prove the platform unbroken; not installed), iOS via the standing `$HOME/athan-gitree/worktrees/ios-build` moved to the lane SHA with its `.env` rewritten to `EXPO_PUBLIC_ENV=local`, `EXPO_PUBLIC_IOS_WIDGETS=1`, `EXPO_IOS_SUFFIX=fleettest`, `EXPO_APP_GROUP=group.com.$BUNDLE.athan.fleettest` (store-id lookups left at placeholder values: the update popup is not under test), then `npx expo prebuild -p ios` and the atlas''s device command: `xcodebuild -workspace ios/Athan.xcworkspace -scheme Athan -configuration Release -destination ''generic/platform=iOS'' -allowProvisioningUpdates CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Automatic DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=$TEAM_ID build` ($TEAM_ID read from the environment at execution, never committed). Assert `plutil -extract CFBundleIdentifier raw <built.app>/Info.plist` prints `com.$BUNDLE.athan.fleettest` before install, then `xcrun devicectl device install app --device IPHONE_UDID <built.app>`. Launch once, confirm the timeline push in `pymobiledevice3 syslog live` (tag `Athan`), drive the customize sheet with the agent-device runner (CLI route per the atlas; its MCP server is broken this session), read one layout at a time by swapping the fleettest app''s widgets in, screenshot, transcribe, and restore the previous lock screen configuration. Write the measured customize-sheet route back into `e2e/device-atlas-iphone-xs.md`. Then merge the lane branch to local uat (no push) and move the ticket to Audit.

## Risks

- A raised nominal truncates instead of shrinking where no floor exists. Every live Text of layout 3 gains the 0.88 floor and layouts 1-2 already floor; the pins hold all of it.
- The stale card''s one-point rise overflows the slot on a short slot. The arithmetic branch in Decisions decides before the code lands; SF Pro line-height arithmetic is deterministic.
